    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/ETS-TRIO-Academic-Advisor--Manchester-Area_JR9619": {
      "title": "ETS/TRIO Academic Advisor, Manchester Area",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nManage and provide comprehensive support services to a middle and high school students across multiple partner schools, including  Manchester Memorial and Central High Schools and Southside and Hillside Middle Schools, Farmington HS and Henry Wilson Middle School. Deliver targeted academic, career, and financial literacy guidance — including financial aid advising — to empower students in achieving educational milestones, including high school graduation and successful college enrollment and completion. Maintain accurate program records and prepare required data submissions and progress reports. Collaborate effectively with school personnel, community organizations, and other stakeholders to support student success. Job Duties: Recruit, select and provide services to TRIO eligible middle school and high school students in target area. Provide educational, career, college, financial literacy and financial aid information. Provide academic support and advising, individually and in groups. Resolve problems of program participants using appropriate advocacy and assistance. Collect data for program and USDE reports. maintain necessary records and files on program participants. Work with school personnel and other professional organizations to increase knowledge and continually update and improve the quality of services to participants. Attend seminars, staff meetings and workshops. Plan, organize and implement college visits, job site tours and other experiences for program participants. Establish contact with parents via workshops, meetings, email and telephone as needed. Complete additional administrative tasks as needed. Requirements: Masters degree, preferably in Education, Counseling or Human Services and two years experience working with middle school and high school students or Bachelors degree and four years of related experience. Experience in using a variety of computer applications. Attention to detail. Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Cover Letter Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration. Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed. Please be advised that this position is supported by external sponsor funding. As such, continued employment in this role is contingent upon the availability of those external funds. If, for any reason, the sponsor funding is reduced or discontinued, employment may be subject to modification or termination in accordance with applicable policies and procedures. The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Compensation Pay Range: $41,890.00 - $74,390.00 The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Prospect-Research-Analyst_JR9565": {
      "title": "Prospect Research Analyst",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Prospect Research Analyst (PRA) is a strategic partner to the University's fundraising program, identifying and evaluating prospective donors, delivering research intelligence, and providing the analytical insight that development teams need to cultivate and solicit major gift donors effectively. The PRA operates with a high degree of autonomy, bringing analytical rigor and professional judgment to estimate giving potential and support the strategic movement of prospects through the donor pipeline. Duties/Responsibilities Research and Prospect Identification (65%) Utilizes advanced research methodologies to gather biographical, financial, and philanthropic data from public records, subscription databases, and internal data systems to assess wealth, giving capacity, and philanthropic propensity. Translates complex financial, biographical, and organizational data into clear, strategically focused research products tailored to the needs of gift officers, University leadership, and volunteer boards. Monitors news, business developments, and other publicly available information to surface timely intelligence that informs development strategy. Supports proactive prospect identification through constituent screenings, giving report reviews, targeted wealth analyses, and other pipeline development initiatives. Partnership and Outreach (15%) Consults with development staff to understand research needs, recommend approaches, and advise on prospect strategy by delivering timely intelligence through research, analysis, and ongoing monitoring of publicly available information. Presents findings and strategic recommendations to a range of audiences, from frontline gift officers to senior leadership. Prospect Management and Portfolio Support (10%) Collaborates with Prospect Management and Pipeline Development colleagues on portfolio reviews, prospect assignments, and related processes, ensuring pools and portfolios are well-populated, strategically aligned, and regularly refreshed. Provides data-informed recommendations that shape cultivation strategies, solicitation planning, and portfolio decisions. Maintains data integrity within the CRM by keeping prospect ratings, assignments, and related prospect information accurate and current.   Research Workflow and Coordination (10%) Manages a personal research queue with a high degree of autonomy, exercising sound judgment to prioritize requests and meet deadlines effectively. Supports research coordination as assigned, including queue management, project intake, and timely delivery of executive research for University leadership. Maintains current knowledge of evolving research resources, tools, and industry best practices to continuously improve the quality and efficiency of research delivery. Requirements Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience: Bachelor’s degree and three years of relevant experience in higher education, nonprofit, advancement, or other roles requiring strong research, writing, and critical thinking skills.   Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Demonstrated expertise in prospect research methodologies, wealth assessment, and donor analysis. Strong analytical skills with the ability to synthesize large volumes of data into strategic insight. Experience with CRM platforms and prospect research tools. Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to distill complex information into clear prose and present findings effectively to audiences ranging from frontline staff to senior leadership. Excellent organizational and time management skills; adept at managing competing priorities in a fast-paced environment. High level of initiative, intellectual curiosity, and commitment to continuous professional development. Sound professional judgment and the ability to manage sensitive and confidential information with discretion. Collaborative and consultative approach to working with development staff and Advancement colleagues. Ability to work independently, adapt readily to change, and contribute positively to a team-oriented culture. Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Cover Letter Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration. Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed. The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Compensation Pay Range: $47,920.00 - $85,410.00 The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Plymouth-State-University/Theatre-Production-Director_JR9612": {
      "title": "Theatre Production Director",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app This person leads a team of creative artists and actors through the process of mounting a theatrical production. Duties/Responsibilities: (10%) Planning the production (10%) Production Meetings (60%) Rehearsal (20%) Technical and Dress Rehearsals Corresponding with pertinent artistic and technical staff relevant to the production towards planning,scheduling, designing scenery, costume, lights, sound, and other elements, plus choreography and music as necessary, and other production aspects as are appropriate. Working with the Director of Theatre and the Silver Center for the Arts to establish a rehearsal schedule for the actors. Being present and working with stage management to lead the rehearsals, sometimes with other members of the creative staff. Being present and providing creative direction at technical rehearsals and dress rehearsals as necessary. Requirements: Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience: Bachelor’s degree in theatre or related field, plus an established resume or portfolio of pertinent work experience. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: A commitment to the growth and education of university students. Patience, compassion, and benevolence with emphasis on best teaching effectiveness as the ultimate goal. Preferred Qualifications: Established Professional Status as evidenced by: Masters Degree or Masters of Fine Arts Affiliation with a Professional Theatre Company or Organization Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Compensation Pay Range: $ 17 per hour Plymouth State University offers high-quality baccalaureate, graduate, and doctoral degree programs. Through research and innovative community partnerships, the University contributes to the economic, social, cultural, and environmental development of the North Country and Lakes Region of New Hampshire and beyond. Plymouth State University (PSU) is transforming the campus to create a first-of-its-kind university holistically organized around integrated clusters. Our goal is to provide a dynamic interdisciplinary and innovative learning environment. Students, faculty, staff, and community will connect to solve real-world challenges that will benefit people and organizations at all levels. We are a residential and comprehensive university with a warm and engaged learning community focused on teaching excellence and regional engagement. The University is located in the heart of the Lakes Region and White Mountains of New Hampshire and serves approximately 4,300 undergraduate and more than 2,000 graduate students. Surrounded by lakes and mountains, PSU’s 170-acre campus provides students with an outstanding natural laboratory for learning and an ideal setting for outdoor recreation. PSU has consistently earned national recognition for its commitment to community service, environmental sustainability, academic excellence, and employee wellness. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Salary Grade: Adjunct Hourly Staff 00 Location: Plymouth"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Keene-State-College/INBRE-Adjunct-Staff_JR9442": {
      "title": "INBRE Adjunct Staff",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app Under the KSC/ NH-INBRE supported component, the incumbent will oversee the daily operation and maintenance of the departmental shared cell culture facility used for both research and instructional purposes. Responsibilities will include ensuring biosafety compliance, maintaining laboratory inventories and supplies, training undergraduate students using the facility for research or course-based activities, and providing essential operational oversight required to sustain a functional and compliant laboratory environment. Duties/Responsibilities Maintenance & Feeding of regular Daphnia cultures - 30% Feeding cultures every M, W and Friday Making Media for cultures Documentation of all day to day activities Making Stock solution for growth Media Organization and cleaning of growth chambers and work area Generation & Maintenance Arsenic Generational Daphnia cultures - 30% Making Stock solution for arsenic growth Media Proper packaging, labelling and disposal of arsenic waste Organ dissections Nucleic acid extractions Generation & Maintenance Chemostats - 20% Proper washing and autoclaving of glass bottles Making media for algal cultures & testing pHs Maintaining continuous algal cultures Support for Undergraduate Research student – 20% Support for ongoing research and course projects Ordering lab supplies and keeping proper records of SDS sheets Attend weekly meetings with the PI to update on lab Training undergraduate students Requirements: Minimum Qualifications Undergraduate degree in Biology or related ﬁeld Basic Laboratory Techniques that include but not limited to Daphnia culture and maintenance, algae culture and maintenance, maintenance and initiation of generational cultures, making growth media and proper documentation of daily activities in lab notebook Optimization of new laboratory protocols Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Cover Letter Contact Information for 3 Professional References Compensation Pay Range: $ 21.56 an hour Please be advised that this position is supported by external sponsor funding. As such, continued employment in this role is contingent upon the availability of those external funds. If, for any reason, the sponsor funding is reduced or discontinued, employment may be subject to modification or termination in accordance with applicable policies and procedures.  Keene State College is located in the scenic Monadnock region of Southwest New Hampshire and is an affiliate of the University System of New Hampshire. Located approximately 2 hours from Boston or Hartford CT, and 4 hours from New York City, the region contains many opportunities to enjoy outdoor recreation, cultural events, and a strong sense of community. To learn more about Keene State College, the University System of New Hampshire, and the Keene community, please visit: https://www.keene.edu , https://www.usnh.edu/ or https://www.ci.keene.nh.us . EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Keene Salary Grade: Adjunct Hourly Staff 00"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire---College-of-Professional-Studies/Assistant-Director-of-Admissions_JR9567": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Admissions",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Assistant Director of Admissions performs duties relevant to the recruitment, admission and counseling of students, resulting in the achievement of enrollment goals established by the university. Position shares with all other admissions officer positions common responsibilities: representing the university to all interested constituencies, reviewing admissions applications, managing recruitment and other recruitment-related duties. This position is exclusive to the Manchester campus, but the individual occupying it will be responsible for reading dual applications to the Durham campus as well. Additional responsibilities include supporting Manchester exclusive campus programming, representing the Manchester campus at recruitment events, and facilitating awareness of the Manchester campus within the public education, non-profit and business/industry community. Duties/Responsibilities Territory management and Recruitment (50%):   Manage the UNH Manchester assigned first-year recruitment territory, which includes independent travel to visit with students, parents, and counselors in their territory. Coordinate recruitment/travel with UNH Durham as needed. Schedule meetings and appointments with high schools, students and other constituencies as well as make hotel, rental car and other travel arrangements. Meet, speak with and counsel prospective students, their parents and/or their guidance counselors to explain pertinent admissions policies and procedures, advise on credentials and answer questions on academic programs and campus life.  Conduct group information sessions that promote and explain the admissions process and the university.  Makes strategic recommendations to improve recruitment and enrollment policies and procedures in order to enroll more first-year students. Outreach to students via phone, email, SMS who are admitted but not enrolled and/or have not yet paid their tuition. Represent the college/university to students, parents, guidance professionals, and members of the general public through programs on campus, at secondary schools, professional organizations, and through high school visits and participation in college fairs and other college programming. Counsel applicants pre- or post-admission decision; perform essential and necessary duties to develop and maintain relationships with constituencies: program evaluation, SMS, email and written correspondence, phone outreach, etc. Use data and research to understand market and student behaviors and inform recruitment strategy within assigned recruitment territory. Track progress toward established enrollment goals within recruitment territory. Responsible for recruitment with NH High Schools for the VLACS program in coordination and collaboration with our UNH online partners. Application review and decisions (40%): Independently read, review, evaluate and process applications for admission and rule on admittance within established guidelines. Participation in file review committees as assigned. Track progress and meet established application review deadlines and goals.  Other areas of focus may include (10%): Staff the UNH Manchester Admissions office when not travelling and assist in answering phone calls, plan and execute information sessions, and managing walk-in prospective students. Lead Special Events for First-Year Recruitment (e.g. Admitted Student Day, Open House, Career Days, etc.). Assist with Supervision of Admissions Student Worker/Wildcat Ambassadors as needed. Responsible for Recruitment for the UNH VLACS Program. Coordinates with UNH Durham on dual campus applications. Assist in staffing of limited admission events and programs. Contribute to admissions planning and/or general office management. Participation in other working groups/committees. Other tasks as assigned.  Requirements Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience: Bachelor’s degree and four years of experience in educational counseling/ administration or Master’s degree in counseling or related field and two years of experience in educational counseling/administration.   Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Demonstrated commitment and experience working with diverse populations (race, ethnicity, sexual orientation, socio-economic status). Evening and weekend work required. Excellent oral and written communication skills required. Excellent personal computer skills required. Excellent analytical ability. Demonstrated appreciation for value and role of higher education. Demonstrated ability to work with families, students, faculty and staff. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple assignments.   Other Requirements: Valid Driver’s License   Preferred Qualifications: Familiarity with college and university admissions policies and procedures. Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Cover Letter Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration. Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed. The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Compensation Pay Range: $43,710.00 - $77,920.00 The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Manchester"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Medical-Assistant_JR9639": {
      "title": "Medical Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app As an integral member of the Medical Services team at The Wellness Center, the Medical Assistant provides both clinical and administrative support to physicians, nurse practitioners, physician assistants, registered nurses, and other healthcare professionals in delivering high-quality, patient-centered care. This position plays a vital role in ensuring efficient clinic operations by supporting direct patient care, assisting with medical procedures, maintaining regulatory and infection control standards, and providing exceptional customer service to a diverse student population. The Medical Assistant functions as an essential member of the interdisciplinary care team while maintaining patient confidentiality and adhering to all applicable healthcare regulations and accreditation standards. Duties/Responsibilities Direct Patient Care (60%) Performs patient check-in, vital signs, height, weight, medication reconciliation, allergy review, and documents past medical history. Clinical Care (15%) Perform a variety of clinical support functions, e.g., in-house point of care testing, administering immunizations, obtaining consent, EKGs, phlebotomy, wheelchair transport, crutch fitting, applying splints, peak flow measurement, spirometry, procedure set-up and assistance, inputting medical information in EMR, limited patient education, etc Administration (15%) Perform various administrative tasks; register patients for their visits, e.g., assign faxes, make appointments, scan documents, answer phone/check voicemail, send/receive faxes, receive prior authorization for medications/imaging orders, obtain credit card/cash/check payments. Quality Checks (10%) Maintain clinical areas, receive and organize supplies, stock exam rooms, record refrigerator temp daily, general equipment maintenance, perform infection control procedures, and perform required quality assurance checks on point of care testing, etc. Requirements Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience: High School One (1) year of medical/clinical assistant experience in a healthcare facility. Required Licenses & Certifications: Certified or Registered Medical Assistant Must be BLS/CPR certified  Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Previous EHR experience. Proficient computer skills required. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with faculty, staff, students, and the general public. Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Compensation Pay Range: $20.42 - 25.35 This is an evergreen posting. While there may not be an immediate opening, we regularly hire for this position throughout the year. Applications are reviewed as opportunities become available. The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham Salary Grade: Adjunct Hourly Staff 00"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Assistant-Strength-and-Conditioning-Coach_JR9461": {
      "title": "Assistant Strength and Conditioning Coach",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app The University of New Hampshire Strength and Conditioning Department is seeking applicants for an assistant strength and conditioning coach. Duties/Responsibilities: Strength and Conditioning Coach for assigned teams, testing and evaluation, communication with sport coaches and athletic training staff. Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree required in Exercise Science or equivalent Prior experience with Div. I Athletics Ability to coach and demonstrate Olympic movements,power lifts, and auxiliary movements Ability to use involving software such as but not limited to Excel & Word Working knowledge of NCAA rules, standards, practices, and procedures Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Cover Letter Contact Information for 3 Professional References Compensation Pay Range: $ 25 per hour The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham Salary Grade: Adjunct Hourly Staff 00"
