    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Social-Media-Producer_JR9509": {
      "title": "Social Media Producer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSummary: The University of New Hampshire is seeking a creative, collaborative, and proactive Social Media Producer to join our central marketing team. Reporting to the Social Media Director, the Social Media Producer is responsible for creating engaging, platform-specific content that brings the UNH experience to life for key audiences, including prospective undergraduate students, current students, and alumni. This highly collaborative role produces multimedia content for UNH social media channels, works closely with student content creators and campus partners, and uses audience insights and performance data to continually strengthen UNH’s social media presence. The ideal candidate has a strong understanding of social media platforms and trends, excellent visual storytelling skills, and experience creating authentic content that connects with audiences while reflecting UNH’s brand and voice. Job Duties/Responsibilities Content Creation, Planning, and Scheduling — 50% Produce and curate high-quality multimedia content, including photos, videos, graphics, and short-form copy, for UNH social media accounts across multiple platforms. Capture live event coverage, behind-the-scenes moments, student experiences, achievements, and other content that brings the UNH experience to life. Plan and schedule social media content in coordination with broader university marketing priorities, campaigns, and audience needs. Collaborate with university departments, student organizations, and external partners to source and create original content that reflects UNH’s brand and resonates with key audiences. Collaboration with Student Workers — 25% Supervise and mentor a team of student workers, coordinating their efforts in capturing and creating social media content that resonates with student audiences. Provide training and guidance on content creation, including photography, videography, and writing for social media, ensuring consistency with the university’s brand and voice. Empower student workers to share their perspectives on campus life, helping provide an authentic and relatable view of the UNH experience. Coordination and Collaboration with Campus Partners — 10% Build and maintain relationships with campus stakeholders to stay abreast of university happenings, priorities, and opportunities for social media content. Align processes with campus partners to improve efficiency, visibility, coordination, and impact. Analytics and Reporting — 10% Monitor social media analytics to understand content performance, audience preferences, and platform trends, using data insights to refine approaches and inform future content. Create monthly, biannual, and campaign-level reports on social media activity, presenting insights to inform team decision-making and optimize content effectiveness. Stay current on social media trends, emerging platforms, tools, and evolving best practices to help ensure UNH remains at the forefront of digital engagement. Community Management — 5% Monitor comments, messages, and brand mentions to foster a positive and interactive online community, actively engaging with audiences as appropriate. Research and implement best practices to improve engagement rates, grow audience reach, and elevate UNH’s social media presence across channels. Minimum Education & Experience Bachelor’s degree in communications, marketing, digital media, or a related field and 2+ years of experience working in social media, including content creation, planning, publishing, and community engagement. Strong proficiency in content creation tools such as Adobe Creative Suite, Canva, and mobile editing applications. Demonstrated experience with video production, photography, and/or graphic design for social media. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with a keen eye for detail and a strong sense of visual storytelling. Knowledge of social media trends, algorithms, platform best practices, and audience behaviors. Ability to manage multiple priorities and collaborate effectively with colleagues and partners across an organization. Experience using social media analytics to evaluate performance and inform content decisions. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in higher education or a similarly complex organization. Experience supervising or mentoring students, interns, or other content creators. Experience creating social media content for multiple audiences and platforms. Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Cover Letter Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration. Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed. The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Compensation Pay Range: $47,920.00 - $85,410.00 The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Keene-State-College/Athletic-Trainer-Keene-State-College-Athletics_JR8753": {
      "title": "Athletic Trainer-Keene State College Athletics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nUnder the direction of the Head Athletic Trainer, this position will provide athletic healthcare services for all varsity level student-athletes. in close cooperation with Head Athletic Trainer, Athletic Training Staff, Team Physicians, and Health Services, assist in the overall service component to Athletics that includes: Prevention, Clinical Evaluation and Diagnosis, Immediate Care Treatment, Rehabilitation & Reconditioning, Organization & Administration and Professional Responsibility. Other duties as assigned. All staff positions on campus support students and will be involved in student-focused activities. Job Duties: Athletic Health Care As an allied health professional, the position requires providing all aspects of student athlete health care focused on evidenced based medicine to include but not limited to the following: Prevention and Health Promotion (injury, illness) Clinical Evaluation and Diagnosis Immediate Care, Acute emergent care Therapeutic Intervention to include Treatment, Rehabilitation & Reconditioning Organization & Administration to include daily EMR Professional responsibility to include maintaining licensure and certification and being current on athlete health care. Other Duties as Assigned . These duties would be assigned by the Head Athletic Trainer and could include, inventory, CPR instructor for athletic staff, online student athletic medical records system super user (Sportsware), etc. Requirements: Entry level Master’s degree in Athletic Training or related field or a Bachelor’s degree in Athletic Training or related field and two years of experience as a certified athletic trainer BOCATC Certification Licensed or eligible for licensure in the state of NH ​ Preferred Qualifications: Post Professional Master’s degree in Athletic Training or a related field Experience in collegiate athletic medicine· CPR Instructor Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Cover Letter Contact Information for 3 Professional References Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration. Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed. This position falls within the collective bargaining unit for the Keene State College Staff Association (KSCSA), an affiliate of the National Education Association of New Hampshire (NEA-NH). Keene State College is located in the scenic Monadnock region of Southwest New Hampshire and is an affiliate of the University System of New Hampshire. Located approximately 2 hours from Boston or Hartford CT, and 4 hours from New York City, the region contains many opportunities to enjoy outdoor recreation, cultural events, and a strong sense of community. To learn more about Keene State College, the University System of New Hampshire, and the Keene community, please visit: https://www.keene.edu , https://www.usnh.edu/ or https://www.ci.keene.nh.us . EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Compensation Pay Range: $40,020.00 - $71,130.00 The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Keene"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Plymouth-State-University/Assistant-Professor-of-Practice--Physical-Therapy_JR9528": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Practice, Physical Therapy",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app The Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) Program in the School of Health at Plymouth State University seeks a full-time 12-month faculty member at the rank of Assistant Professor of Practice to support delivery of the professional curriculum. This position is primarily responsible for teaching, laboratory instruction, and coordination of selected courses across the curriculum, as well as participation in integrated clinical education experiences The faculty member will contribute to a highly integrated, practice-oriented curriculum that combines didactic instruction with early and progressive clinical experiences, including participation in the program’s pro bono clinic. Responsibilities include course coordination, student assessment, and engagement in program assessment and continuous improvement processes consistent with accreditation standards. The position requires maintenance of contemporary clinical expertise and engagement in scholarship appropriate to a teaching-focused faculty role. Duties/Responsibilities Teaching and Course Coordination - 70% Serve as primary instructor and/or course coordinator for assigned courses, including but not limited to Clinical & Functional Anatomy, Musculoskeletal Conditions, Patient/Client Management V, and Movement Systems Deliver classroom and laboratory instruction emphasizing clinical reasoning, examination, and intervention skills Develop and maintain course materials, assessments, and learning activities aligned with program outcomes and accreditation standards Evaluate student performance and provide timely, constructive feedback Provide advising and mentoring for Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) students and undergraduate Allied Health students as assigned Profession, University, School and Program Service - 20% Participate in program assessment, curriculum review, and strategic planning processes Contribute to accreditation-related activities and documentation Engage in faculty meetings and program initiatives Participate in professional, university, school, and community service activities, including shared governance and engagement with professional organizations Clinical Scholarship - 10% Engage in clinical scholarship that advances the profession of physical therapy, including integration of evidence into teaching and dissemination of clinical expertise Maintain contemporary expertise through clinical practice, continuing education, and professional engagement Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) or equivalent entry-level physical therapy degree Licensed or eligible for licensure as a physical therapist in the State of New Hampshire Completion of, or Progress toward, a terminal academic doctoral degree (e.g., PhD, EdD, ScD) consistent with programmatic needs and accreditation requirement Minimum of 8 years of contemporary clinical experience in physical therapy practice Demonstrated effectiveness in teaching in a graduate professional physical therapy education setting, including classroom and laboratory instruction Demonstrated teaching experience in areas including but not limited to clinical anatomy, orthopedic pathology, and management of musculoskeletal, complex and cardiopulmonary cases. Required Licenses & Certifications: Licensed to practice Physical Therapy in the State of New Hampshire Preferred Qualifications: Board certification in a clinical specialty relevant for the expected teaching assignment through the American Board of Physical Therapy Specialties (ABPTS) (e.g., Orthopedic or Cardiopulmonary Clinical Specialist) Skills & Competencies: Strong clinical reasoning and problem-solving skills in musculoskeletal and cardiopulmonary physical therapy practice Ability to effectively communicate complex concepts in both classroom and laboratory settings Strong organizational, time management, and interpersonal skills Ability to mentor, instruct, and evaluate undergraduate and graduate-level students in academic and clinical environments Ability to integrate evidence-based practice and contemporary clinical knowledge into teaching and learning activities Commitment to inclusive, student-centered learning environments Ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, staff, and clinical partners Ability to adapt teaching strategies to support diverse learners and dynamic educational settings Ability to perform the physical tasks associated with laboratory instruction and clinical skills demonstration Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Cover Letter Contact Information for 3 Professional References Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration. Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed. Compensation Pay Range: $95,000 - $100,000 The rank of the selected candidate will depend upon the candidate’s qualifications. Plymouth State University offers high-quality baccalaureate, graduate, and doctoral degree programs. Through research and innovative community partnerships, the University contributes to the economic, social, cultural, and environmental development of the North Country and Lakes Region of New Hampshire and beyond. Plymouth State University (PSU) is transforming the campus to create a first-of-its-kind university holistically organized around integrated clusters. Our goal is to provide a dynamic interdisciplinary and innovative learning environment. Students, faculty, staff, and community will connect to solve real-world challenges that will benefit people and organizations at all levels. We are a residential and comprehensive university with a warm and engaged learning community focused on teaching excellence and regional engagement. The University is located in the heart of the Lakes Region and White Mountains of New Hampshire and serves approximately 4,300 undergraduate and more than 2,000 graduate students. Surrounded by lakes and mountains, PSU’s 170-acre campus provides students with an outstanding natural laboratory for learning and an ideal setting for outdoor recreation. PSU has consistently earned national recognition for its commitment to community service, environmental sustainability, academic excellence, and employee wellness. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Salary Grade: Faculty 01 Location: Plymouth"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire---Franklin-Pierce-School-of-Law/Career-Services-Director--UNH-Law_JR7549": {
      "title": "Career Services Director, UNH Law",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nReporting to the Assistant Dean of Career and Academic Advising, the Director of Career and Academic Advising plays a key role in the delivery of the full range of services supporting law students and alumni in their career and academic development. The Director provides significant input into the overall strategy of the Office of Career & Academic Advising, which provides service to residential & hybrid JD students as well as residential and online graduate students.  In addition to meeting 1-on-1 with students, the Director leads the development of multiple programs in support of student success.   Duties/Responsibilities Strategic/Operational Planning (10%) In collaboration with the Assistant Dean, set career and academic advising strategic vision/plan in accordance with the law school’s priorities; develop strategies for all law school student categories including residential and hybrid JD students, residential and online graduate students, and alumni. Develop new services and programs for students and alumni, with a specific focus on the hybrid student population and students with an interest in public service. Work with the employer outreach team to develop strategies for increasing student employment opportunities Serve as primary liaison to external organizations, including Equal Justice Works, Skadden Fellowship, Intellectual Property Owners Association, American Intellectual Property Law Association, and similar organizations. Individual Career & Academic Counseling and Student Outreach (50%) Provide individual counseling on academic and job search strategies to all student cohorts Assist students in developing job search strategies: develop action plans and identify experiences that reflect competencies required for a position. Identify experience, interests, and skills as they relate to various legal careers Assist students in preparing professional documents and application materials; conduct student mock interviews and networking to expand student skill development In collaboration with the Student Life team, serve as partner to student groups, working with them on programming for the year and ensure that student leaders are kept apprised of opportunities. Program Development & Workshop Planning and Execution (30%) Co-teach 1-credit “Legal Profession” course to residential (Fall) and hybrid (Summer) 1L students Develop and deliver career and professional development programs for each student cohort, with a specific focus on the hybrid student population and students with an interest in public service careers Administer the Loan Repayment Assistance Program, Student Professional Development Fund, and similar programs Develop and execute a clerkship program. Administration and Data Gathering (10%) Assist with gathering and maintaining student data and information.  Maintain data integrity and help to compile annual employment outcomes required by ABA, NALP, and others. Assist in developing and executing protocols surrounding data management and office functions using the 12Twenty System Input data accurately into 12Twenty CRM system Collaborate with Admissions, Alumni Affairs, Academic Affairs, Students Life, and other law school departments; other offices to deliver the highest quality service to students. Requirements Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience Must be able to use independent judgement and discretion. Requires Bachelor’s Degree in a related field. JD and/or other advanced professional degree strongly preferred. Requires 5+ years legal practice, career counseling or legal recruiting experience. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Requires knowledge of nationwide market for law school graduates, including both attorney and non-attorney career paths. Requires superior interpersonal skills, including the ability to communicate professionally with highly motivated and professionally successful student body, employers, faculty, and professional staff. Must be able to use independent judgement and discretion. Must be able to create an inclusive environment, encourage valuing of persons from different backgrounds and promoting a law school atmosphere that assures equitable treatment for all persons.   Must be comfortable adapting to technology and open to learning new technological solutions, including the use of AI. Other Requirements: Position is full-time onsite in Concord, NH. Preferred Qualifications: Familiarity with Career Services CRM systems such as 12Twenty or Symplicity Prior experience counseling professionals in career related matters Prior experience working as an attorney Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Cover Letter Contact Information for 3 Professional References Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration. Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed. The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Compensation Pay Range: $54,990.00 - $98,150.00 The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Concord"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Keene-State-College/Senior-Administrative-Assistant_JR8984": {
      "title": "Senior Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThis position serves as the first point of contact for students, faculty, families and staff and provides high level administrative support to academic departments within Academic Affairs. Performs diverse, responsible, and complex office support functions including procurement, budgeting and financial transaction reconciliation, assisting with events, communicating and coordinating information using independent judgment, problem-solving skills and initiative to determine approach of action to take in non-routine situation, by interpreting departmental guidelines, KSC and USNH policies and procedures. All staff positions on campus support students and will be involved in student-focused activities. Duties/Responsibilities Administrative Support (75%)  Provide administrative support for academic departments including responding to electronic inquiries, answering phones, entering course schedules for each department, offering support with completing paperwork, assisting in hiring and managing of student workers and adjunct staff and adjunct faculty as needed. Manage the ebb and flow of continuous deadlines, procedures, student employment, and changes in faculty. Assist with the onboarding of new department chairs, faculty, staff, adjunct faculty/staff, and students in all areas of ever-changing processes and programs. Produce various data, forms, reports for the departments and deans as necessary. Schedule and coordinate meetings as necessary. Responsible for departmental communications to students. Collaborate, provide direction, and assist department chairs, coordinators, faculty, students, prospective families, the public, outside reviewers, and colleagues across the campus community. Respond to all inquiries through all matters of communication. Create, maintain, utilize, and analyze information from databases for student and faculty information. Communicate information to the Dean, Department Chair’s and the Provost Office where appropriate. Post electronic and physical announcements for class cancellations and room changes (online and physical location). Establish and manage e-filing systems for departments using judgment and knowledge of office requirements. Provide ad hoc reports as necessary, i.e. Accreditation and program review Order office supplies, complete maintenance request forms as necessary Assist with updating department social media page as applicable Other duties as assigned   Business Operations (15%) Assist with the overall management of the business operations, travel, payable and receivable, purchasing, budget management and control, payroll, and inventory control. Assist with management of academic department budgets on a day-to-day basis. Forecasting budget requirements and obligations to ensure maintenance of adequate funding. Work with KSC finance team and USNH Procurement to secure departmental purchases. Serve as the departmental point person with the KSC finance department and Sponsored Projects and Research.   Special Projects, Events (10%)  In collaboration with department faculty coordinate workshops, meetings, special events, marketing/promotions. This includes but is not limited to the following: event costing, purchases, food, rentals, technical support, security, reimbursements, vendors, promotions, travel, and accommodations. Implement outreach activities for the campus at large and/or local community. Requirements Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience: High school graduation/equivalent and four years of office support experience of increasing responsibility or any combination of experience and higher education equal to four years. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Ability to rapidly shift task priorities based on urgency of departments’, faculty’s, and students’ needs. Demonstrated organizational, analytical, and problem-solving skills, attention to detail. Effective written and oral communication skills. The ability to maintain appropriate confidentiality of sensitive information. Other Requirements: Proven experience formatting and editing letters and documents. Experience with tasks involving increased responsibility and requiring discretion and independent judgment. Proven experience as a successful team member including interest and ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with faculty, staff, students and the general public. Proficiency with computer applications, including MS Word, Excel, Outlook, Access and relational databases. Demonstrated experience processing financials including accounts payable/receivable. Preferred Qualifications: Associate’s degree or Bachelor’s degree Work experience in college/university environment Experience with Workday or similar HR/Finance/Student System  Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Cover Letter Contact Information for 3 Professional References Anticipated hourly rate is $21.00-23.00 an hour depending upon experience and internal equity. Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration. Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed. This position falls within the collective bargaining unit for the Keene State College Administrative Staff Association (KSCASA), an affiliate of the National Education Association of New Hampshire (NEA-NH). Keene State College is located in the scenic Monadnock region of Southwest New Hampshire and is an affiliate of the University System of New Hampshire. Located approximately 2 hours from Boston or Hartford CT, and 4 hours from New York City, the region contains many opportunities to enjoy outdoor recreation, cultural events, and a strong sense of community. To learn more about Keene State College, the University System of New Hampshire, and the Keene community, please visit: https://www.keene.edu , https://www.usnh.edu/ or https://www.ci.keene.nh.us . EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Compensation Pay Range: $17.57 - $28.96 The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Keene"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Plymouth-State-University/All-New-England-Band-Festival-Coordinator_JR9513": {
      "title": "All New England Band Festival Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app The All New England Band Festival Coordinator plans the event and coordinates with all parties involved, including the Silver Center staff, the School of Integrated Liberal Arts, the School of Education, and participating schools. This is an hourly staff position. Duties/Responsibilities The All New England Band Festival Coordinator is responsible for inviting a guest conductor and obtaining approval for the conductor fee by the School administrative staff. Contract information needs to be provided to the School at least 1 month prior to the event. Draft a proposed event budget for approval by the School administrative staff. Facilitate event needs with the Silver Center Director and Silver Center Events Coordinator. Communicate set up needs and event parking at least 3 weeks prior to event. Provide a list (with links) of music needed for event. Scan in parts for bands to send to each participant. Oversee student band fellows and music education students assisting with event. Enter hours worked weekly. Manage registration of participating schools and relay invoice information to School administrative staff. Requirements: Minimum Education & Experience Bachelor’s required Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Symphonic band conducting experience. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s preferred Compensation Pay Range: $50 /hour Plymouth State University offers high-quality baccalaureate, graduate, and doctoral degree programs. Through research and innovative community partnerships, the University contributes to the economic, social, cultural, and environmental development of the North Country and Lakes Region of New Hampshire and beyond. Plymouth State University (PSU) is transforming the campus to create a first-of-its-kind university holistically organized around integrated clusters. Our goal is to provide a dynamic interdisciplinary and innovative learning environment. Students, faculty, staff, and community will connect to solve real-world challenges that will benefit people and organizations at all levels. We are a residential and comprehensive university with a warm and engaged learning community focused on teaching excellence and regional engagement. The University is located in the heart of the Lakes Region and White Mountains of New Hampshire and serves approximately 4,300 undergraduate and more than 2,000 graduate students. Surrounded by lakes and mountains, PSU’s 170-acre campus provides students with an outstanding natural laboratory for learning and an ideal setting for outdoor recreation. PSU has consistently earned national recognition for its commitment to community service, environmental sustainability, academic excellence, and employee wellness. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Salary Grade: Adjunct Hourly Staff 00 Location: Plymouth"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Project-Director-II_JR9342": {
      "title": "Project Director II",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Project Director II will work at the Institute on Disability on 1-2 externally-funded research projects about interventions to support young adults with intellectual and developmental disabilities. One study is focused on comparing two delivery-approaches of a transportation intervention, and the other is focused on a peer-delivered mental health intervention. The Project Director II will manage projects, supervise research assistants, collect, manage, and analyze data for both projects, and contribute to dissemination. This potential is not considered essential staff (i.e., not required to work during curtailment). Duties/Responsibilities Project Management and Coordination (55%) Conduct and coordinate data collection for two funded studies by communicating with local research sites and the multi-site team. Attend team leadership meetings Train sites on the Ready to Ride intervention and peer support Complete administrative tasks to prepare intervention materials (e.g., formatting materials, occasionally printing, ordering supplies, etc.) Ensure all research protocols are conducted in a standardized manner, across multiple research sites. This includes coordination with project managers and researchers across multiple universities through email, phone, and virtual meetings. Data Management (10%) Securely manage all incoming data for both projects. This includes data entry, database management, and REDCap management and database development. Training and Supervision (10%) Supervise hourly research assistants Train interventionists across research sites in the Boston area and Manchester Observe interventionist performance, document fidelity, and provide additional training to support fidelity, as needed. Data Collection (25%) Administer standardized assessments for both projects. This includes observational assessments and self-report assessments. Observe in-person delivery of the Mental Health StepUp Peer intervention and take detailed notes in a structured format. Dissemination (10%) Prepare, publish and disseminate reports and other written materials on results and conclusions of the project and other relevant topics. Have an opportunity to write up findings and be an author on presentations and/or manuscripts. Requirements Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience: Bachelor’s Degree Experience with individuals with intellectual and/or developmental disabilities Ability to follow standardized protocols to administer assessments and complete observations Strong attention to detail Strong communication skills Willingness to travel to the Boston area and Manchester, NH during the work week (i.e., availability at least 2-3 days/week between 9am and 5pm) Transportation study: Travel is expected to occur ~30-40 times/year Mental health study: Travel is expected to occur to occur ~2 times/week Travel costs will be reimbursed Ability to manage time and complete tasks in a hybrid work environment.    Preferred Qualifications: Clinical training (position is open to students working towards clinical or education licensure) Experience with qualitative coding Experience with data management Master's degree Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Cover Letter Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration. Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed. Please be advised that this position is supported by external sponsor funding. As such, continued employment in this role is contingent upon the availability of those external funds. If, for any reason, the sponsor funding is reduced or discontinued, employment may be subject to modification or termination in accordance with applicable policies and procedures.  The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Compensation Pay Range: $54,990.00 - $98,150.00 The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Director-of-UNH-Wildcat-Productions_JR9447": {
      "title": "Director of UNH Wildcat Productions",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Director of UNH Wildcat Productions serves as a member of the UNH Athletics Marketing and Communications team within the External Relations unit. This position is responsible for leading all aspects of live event production, video board operations, digital broadcasts, and fan engagement programming for UNH Athletics and select university events. The Director oversees the planning, execution, and enhancement of in-venue entertainment and live broadcasts while supporting the strategic goals of UNH Athletics through innovative storytelling, engaging content, and high-quality production experiences. The position reports to the Associate Athletic Director for Marketing and Communications and supervises full-time staff, student employees, and game-day production personnel. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Lead all aspects of videoboard, broadcast, and production room operations for UNH Athletics events and select university events, including commencement ceremonies, concerts, conferences, and special events.   Produce and direct live broadcasts for ESPN+, streaming platforms, and other digital and linear distribution partners.   Develop, implement, and enhance in-game entertainment experiences, including videoboard content, special effects, fan engagement initiatives, promotional elements, and sponsored activations.   Collaborate with Athletics Marketing and Communications staff to create and deploy promotional videos, hype videos, public service announcements, highlights, replay packages, and other multimedia content.   Oversee the creation and execution of game presentation run-of-show scripts and broadcast production plans.   Hire, train, schedule, and supervise professional staff, student employees, freelance personnel, and game-day production crews, including camera operators, replay operators, graphics personnel, and broadcast talent.   Manage production budgets and equipment purchases while maintaining operational efficiency and production quality.   Ensure all production systems, equipment, and facilities are properly maintained and operational.   Serve as the primary production contact for external events utilizing videoboard and broadcast resources within UNH Athletics facilities.   Work collaboratively with Wildcat Sports Properties to fulfill sponsorship obligations and integrate partner activations into game presentation and broadcast programming.   Partner with coaches, student-athletes, and athletics staff to develop creative content that promotes UNH Athletics and enhances fan engagement.   Ensure compliance with NCAA, conference, university, and applicable state and federal regulations.   Perform other duties as assigned in support of the mission and goals of UNH Athletics.   Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree in television production, sports management, journalism, communications, media production, or a related field.   Three years of professional experience in sports production, live event production, broadcasting, or a related field.   Demonstrated experience producing and directing live broadcasts and event productions.   Experience supervising staff, students, or production crews.   Strong organizational, communication, and project management skills.   Ability to work evenings, weekends, and occasional travel as required.   Preferred Qualifications Master's degree in a related field.   Experience producing Division I collegiate athletics broadcasts. (Derived from the role's athletics production focus; if preferred, this can be omitted because it is not explicitly listed in the source.) Proficiency with industry-standard production technologies and software, including video editing, graphics, replay, and live production systems.   Experience with Adobe Creative Cloud products, including Photoshop and InDesign, as well as broadcast production platforms and streaming technologies.   Working Conditions This position requires frequent evening and weekend work in support of athletics events and special productions. The successful candidate must be able to manage multiple projects simultaneously in a fast-paced, deadline-driven environment while maintaining a high standard of professionalism and customer service.   Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Cover Letter Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration. Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed. The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Compensation Pay Range: $57,590.00 - $102,850.00 The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Quality-Assurance-Monitor_JR9556": {
      "title": "Quality Assurance Monitor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nUnder the direction of the Project Director III, the Project Director I is responsible for conducting quality assurance and certification reviews for NH Department of Health & Human Services (DHHS) youth residential treatment program sites, including visit documentation, adhering to all QA protocols, completing reports and other documentation, and following safety and confidentiality protocols. Duties/Responsibilities Quality assurance and certification reviews (100%) Schedule and conduct quality monitoring reviews. Facilitate interviews, in collaboration with state evaluators. Create outcome reports based on the results of the visits and interview feedback, identifying recommendations and areas for follow up, and sharing recommendations with residential providers. Monitor necessary follow-up identified in the outcome report. Actively participate in meetings with project partners. Assist in the development of tools for the quality monitoring process. Provide feedback regarding the quality monitoring process and best practices. Support the development of tools and processes for the quality monitoring process. Maintain data collection requirements.   Requirements Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience: Master's degree in appropriate academic discipline and three years of experience related to project specialization, or bachelor's degree in appropriate academic discipline and five years of experience related to project specialization. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Ability to independently design, conduct, and track data collection activities. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Willingness to travel on a regular basis both in state and out of state. Ability to maintain confidentiality and adhere to ethical standards when handling highly sensitive information. Other Requirements: Ability to travel for both in-state and out of state reviews Preferred Qualifications: Experience working in or with NH DHHS service systems. Experience working in or with mental health programs, especially  with children and youth. Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Cover Letter Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration. Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed. The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Compensation Pay Range: $47,920.00 - $85,410.00 The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Associate-Director-of-Development--Athletics_JR9500": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Development, Athletics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Associate Director of Development (ADoD), Athletics helps drive major gift efforts for UNH Athletics, strengthening a high-caliber fundraising program that reflects the University’s culture, mission, goals, and evolving strategic plans. The incumbent will focus primarily on managing a portfolio of major gift prospects capable of making philanthropic contributions in support of the priorities set by the Athletics Director (AD). In addition to partnering with leadership and stakeholders across UNH Athletics, they will also collaborate with many colleagues across the Development team and University Advancement. Beyond personal outreach and interactions, they will coordinate strategic communications, events, and other initiatives as needed to identify, qualify, cultivate, solicit, engage and steward prospects to motivate them toward major giving in support of Athletics. The incumbent will embrace goal-oriented outcomes and be an entrepreneurial, strategic, and creative thinker who is capable of building and expanding relationships with constituents in ways that have a quantifiable impact on philanthropic achievement. They will have a proven track record in fundraising or a closely related field of expertise, and will possess outstanding interpersonal competencies, ability to effectively manage projects/priorities, and be highly motivated, organized and detail oriented.    Job Duties/Responsibilities: Front-Line Fundraising - 90% Maintain a robust portfolio of major gift prospects consisting of Athletics constituents, including alumni, donors, and friends of UNH Athletics; maintain frequent contact with these individuals and organizations to build relationships and increase philanthropic support. Conduct up to 150 visits each year with prospects and potential prospects via video conferencing, phone, and/or in-person; meeting this activity goal will require travel across the state, region, and, on occasion, the U.S. When needed, engage the Athletics Director, coaches, and staff in these visits. Craft meaningful funding proposals to facilitate major gifts and multi-year commitments that align with the donors’ and the Athletics Director’s fundraising and/or strategic priorities. Solicit gifts of all levels for Athletics, with a focus on major gifts, from assigned prospects and other donors or potential donors to achieve annual revenue goals. Assist the entire Development team with achieving alumni participation goals, overall for the university and for Athletics. This will require engagement in key campaigns such as the annual (603) Challenge and year-end pushes. Facilitate pipeline movement across all laterals of the Development spectrum (Annual Giving, Leadership Giving, Major Giving, and Planned Giving), working closely with colleagues to successfully transition prospects. Qualify new prospects and disqualify prospects for leadership level giving by conducting a series of steps that deem their affinity and inclination to engage philanthropically at that level. Steward prospects and donors through their philanthropic journey with UNH Athletics with the goal of maximizing their donor potential. Utilize CRM database, reports, and other available technologies to efficiently manage, engage and expand your portfolio. Planning & Coordination - 10% Plan and execute major gift communications and marketing for Athletics in partnership with colleagues across the Development team, utilizing all available channels (mail, phone, email, social media, etc.). Plan and facilitate major gift cultivation and stewardship activities (events, programs, and other touchpoints) in partnership with Development colleagues. Consult with leadership and staff across UNH Athletics on above tactics, engaging them in strategies when possible and ensuring efforts align with the Athletics Director’s priorities and vision. Partner with the Director of Development for Athletics to determine annual goals for all individual and unit level metrics. Regularly monitor progress through reports and ensure data is recorded timely and accurately; work to ensure these goals are all achieved each year. Work collaboratively across all Development and Advancement teams to support both the division and university in its fundraising goals and strategic plans and to ensure that leadership giving strategies align with overall fundraising and engagement strategies and vice versa. Participate in events, programs, meetings, and initiatives that support UNH and Athletics as directed by Development, Advancement, and the Athletics Director. Requirements Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience: Minimum of 5 years of fundraising experience or more years of experience in a relevant field (sales, business development, account/relationship management, marketing and/or public relations).   Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Bachelor's degree Demonstrated understanding of the relevance of philanthropy and Development expertise Ability to communicate effectively, both verbally and in writing, about fundraising support; requires the ability to build rapport in an open, friendly, and accepting way, listen attentively and change the thinking of, or gain acceptance of, others in varied situations. Exceptionally strong interpersonal skills and experience interacting with internal and external constituents who are diverse in characteristics such as age, education level, race, gender identity and expression, ability, and socioeconomic backgrounds in a culturally competent and supportive manner. Exceptionally strong organizational skills and ability to juggle and prioritize a multitude of projects/tasks. Orientation as a team player and demonstrated strength at partnering with peers, management, and leadership and collaborating across diverse university units and departments. Demonstrated understating of the responsibility to maintain sensitive information and appreciation of ethics and compliance. Openness to travel on behalf of UNH for donor/prospect visits or as the university's representative, including local, regional, and domestic trips. Exceptionally strong analytical skills and experience working in a metrics-driven environment. Proficiency in database technologies and Microsoft Office and technological/data acumen. Commitment to the values of diversity, equity, inclusion, and advancement Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of the fundraising profession, theories, and standards Knowledge of philanthropy policies, practices, and systems Familiarity with a university setting and fundraising campaigns Proficiency in database technologies and Microsoft Office Experience with portfolio and volunteer engagement Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Cover Letter Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration. Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed. About the UNH Foundation ( UNHF) and UNH Development: Established in 1989, the UNHF exists to build private philanthropic support for the university with the goal of strengthening programs and supporting students, faculty and staff. The UNH Development team is the fundraising arm of the UNHF, working to advance the mission of the university by inspiring giving among alumni, parents/families, friends, employees, corporations, and foundations. Our donor-centered approach connects stakeholders’ passions and philanthropic goals to funding opportunities at UNH, resulting in meaningful and lasting impacts across the university. The Development team is structured to ensure every level of the donor pyramid is poised for growth and success in the short and long-term, with staff focused on annual giving, leadership giving, major giving, principal and planned giving, and foundation relations. Further, most team members are assigned to fundraise for a specific area of the university, supported by Development leadership and operations staff who work across the various teams. Our team is ambitious about the potential of our fundraising outcomes, embraces diverse perspectives, commits to professional growth, operates with integrity and collaborates in every way possible. Please join us!    Hybrid Workplace Expectation: University Advancement has implemented a hybrid work model, and this is a hybrid position. The expectation is that employees reside within reasonable distance to the Durham, NH campus (under three hours) so they are available to come to campus as often as business needs dictate, which vary depending on the position and assigned areas. The hiring manager will clarify exact expectation of in-person versus remote working time for each specific position. The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Compensation Pay Range: $66,480.00 - $118,860.00 The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Plymouth-State-University/Administrative-Specialist_JR8496-1": {
      "title": "Administrative Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nUnder general supervision of the School Director, the Administrative Specialist will provide administrative support (academic, HR, Finance, and other) to faculty, staff, and students within the School. The Administrative Specialist will ensure the smooth operations of the School through knowledge and appropriate application of institutional policy, procedures, rules, and regulations. This position is critical to providing stability to the operational structure of the School. Plymouth State University’s academic programs are organized into six Schools. Each one consists of faculty, staff, and students associated with multiple degree programs and academic disciplines. Administrative Specialists will provide administrative leadership in collaboration with directors and support assistants in their assigned School, but will also work with colleagues in other Schools and with support staff across the University to ensure student and program success. The Director, the Administrative Specialist, and the AOM will work together as a team, and as such, the Administrative Specialist duties might not be exclusive to what is outlined in this description. This role is dynamic and requires a willingness to be flexible. Duties/Responsibilities Academic and Financial Support (70%) Serve as the primary point of contact for the School and its programs to non-School offices and services such as Admissions, ACAC, Communications and Marketing, Advancement, Student Life, the Registrar’s Office, Student Financial Services, etc. to promote operational efficiency and enhanced communication.  Be part of the monthly leadership meetings with OAA.  Together with the Director, take care of operational and academic needs of the School, including: Serving as a primary contact to OAA for operational tasks and problem solving Planning the schedule of courses, including faculty and TL assignments Building faculty workload and overload reports to OAA Managing low-enrolled courses, including coordinating with OAA, and communication with the Registrar’s Office, instructors, and affected students when courses are cancelled Assisting with the creation of School and programmatic work plans Assisting with academic/program support activities such as program reviews, fees management, and other academic projects Supporting the onboarding of new full-time and part-time faculty Planning monthly School-wide meetings and any School retreats done during the academic year (with the support of the Academic Operations Manager) Providing oversight of the budget Managing budget requests and helping to write and facilitate any SPA/MOU contracts appropriate to the School. Manage other operational responsibilities to support the School, including: Providing schedules to the AOM for entering into the PSU scheduling platform  Reviewing the schedule entered in the PSU system before registration begins.  Developing and maintaining an on-line repository of records required to align program accreditation and other assessment requirements.  Develop/managing School’s SharePoint site to facilitate internal communications and project management.  Coordinating the budget planning & management processes with assistance from the AOM.   As the AOM and the Administrative Specialist will likely be located in different buildings, manage expected responsibilities associated with the assigned location Student Support (20%) Potentially serve as an Academic Advisor to new and continuing majors in appropriate programs. The Provost or Associate Provost will review/approve of this role for any individual Administrative Specialist. Support and manage curricular changes along with the school Director Keep current with best practices of, and tools for, supporting students Serve as signatory authority (together with the School Director) for student requests, change of majors, academic minor/certificate declarations, etc.  Either serve as the first point of contact or support the Director on issues such as students and faculty complaints, fair grading and academic integrity violations, etc. Admissions, Enrollment Management, and Retention (10%) Support the participation of program faculty in admissions events Participate in admissions events such as Open Houses, Accepted Student Days, etc. (which might happen outside regular work hours) Support the Undergraduate and Graduate Admissions, Enrollment, and Retention initiatives of the School. Work with Admissions on student materials and admissions tours in collaboration with the School faculty and staff.  Along with the Director, plan for course/enrollment needs for graduate and undergraduate offerings Requirements Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience: High School diploma and at least two years of administrative support experience in any setting A well-rounded selection of as many of the KSAs/Competencies (soft skills) listed below as possible Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Excellent interpersonal skills and willingness to collaborate and work with others, including faculty, staff, administration, students, and external stakeholders. Ability to work collaboratively and communicate effectively with faculty, staff, students, administrators, and external stakeholders Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships across campus and with the general public. Ability to work both independently and as a part of a team Ability to work in a high-volume, fast-paced environment that experiences frequent changes and interruptions Strong problem-solving skills Strong customer service skills Appropriate professional behavior Ability to maintain confidentiality about sensitive issues Effective written and communication skills Ability to understand and support the management of budgets Proficiency using computers and standard software such as the Microsoft 365 Suite Ability and willingness to learn Enterprise Resource Planning (such as Banner and Workday) and other applications needed for the performance of School support duties Self-motivation and commitment to continued self-improvement   Preferred Qualifications: A high school diploma with five years of support experience, OR a Bachelor’s-or-higher degree with academic support experience in a Higher Education setting Office management experience Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Cover Letter Contact Information for 3 Professional References Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration. Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed. Plymouth State University offers high-quality baccalaureate, graduate, and doctoral degree programs. Through research and innovative community partnerships, the University contributes to the economic, social, cultural, and environmental development of the North Country and Lakes Region of New Hampshire and beyond. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Compensation Pay Range: $20.15 - $33.15 The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Plymouth"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Keene-State-College/Help-Desk-Shift-Supervisor_JR8978": {
      "title": "Help Desk Shift Supervisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAs part of the Client Services team in Enterprise Technology & Services, and working under general supervision, you use advanced industry knowledge and USNH policies to support various hardware and software needs. You serve as the main contact for clients, communicating clearly with non-technical users. Your responsibilities include working independently or with others to handle essential user support tasks—such as deploying, monitoring, and maintaining Windows and Mac devices; troubleshooting network and printing problems; managing computer lifecycles and IT assets; configuring systems; and replacing computers. You deliver direct support to faculty and staff regarding computers, mobile devices, account access, networking, cloud storage, security, and data management. You also provide training and documentation on systems, software, policies, and procedures. In addition, you manage or contribute to projects that are key to the department's mission, and you actively seek opportunities to advance your technical and managerial skills. Duties/Responsibilities Customer Support (50%) Consult with clients both on-site and remotely, collaborate with the service desk and team members regarding information technology needs, respond promptly to issues, and resolve assigned problems. Assist in analyzing technical challenges and developing effective solutions, referring complex cases appropriately. Utilize enterprise ticketing systems and associated workflows efficiently. Oversee software installation and maintenance by selecting, testing, installing, and maintaining software applications and network resources. Employ critical problem-solving skills, develop and document solutions and workarounds, research and address complex issues independently, and prioritize tasks effectively in a fast-paced environment.  Demonstrate strong business relationship-building and communicate effectively with the user community. Advise clients on the implementation of suitable technologies; address and resolve their IT concerns as assigned; analyze complex IT problems and coordinate additional assistance when necessary; consider and recommend comprehensive solutions for a diverse audience.  Ensure security compliance by adhering to established policies and procedures: monitor system security, investigate issues, and recommend corrective actions such as assisting with operation and maintenance of application software security facilities. Maintain up-to-date knowledge of all USNH IT Security recommendations. Resource Lifecycle Management (15%) Maintain precise hardware asset inventory and endpoint records, including physical audits. Set up new computers, configure domain accounts, update Active Directory for systems management, and create user accounts, including login and printer setup support. Assist with computer configuration and procurement according to USNH policies. Collaborate with Endpoint Engineering to resolve compliance issues and eliminate vulnerabilities. Coordinate surplus pickup for end-of-life assets and manage information databases. Documentation (10%) Assess and address documentation requirements, including the development of supporting materials for newly implemented or updated application software; ensure documentation is accurate, consistent, and presented in a manner accessible to clients. Conduct research to resolve complex technical issues and document solutions and workarounds. Communicate major resolutions to relevant stakeholders as appropriate. Utilize the enterprise ticketing system to record incidents, solutions, and workarounds, while analyzing trends and referencing historical data to enhance client support. Collaborate effectively with colleagues across the University System of NH  as needed. Provide subject matter expertise during crisis situations, such as virus outbreaks or disaster recovery efforts, and offer backup support to the team when required. Employ existing resources, including remote support tools, to assist clients who are off-campus or unable to be present in person. Strategic and Project Planning (10%) Assist with strategic and project planning, including technology refreshes for teaching labs, classrooms, and end-user assets. Recommend equipment purchases when necessary due to age or failure. Manage and track loaner equipment. Support IT project execution by advising, collaborating, documenting, and contributing to ET&S initiatives. Supervision (10%) Guide and support student workers by mentoring them and providing training. Create documentation and instructional materials to help enhance their skills and broaden their knowledge. Participate in the assessment and review the performance of student workers. Other duties as assigned (5%) Stay up to date with new technologies, including remote support tools, security measures, and productivity applications relevant to your work. This also includes supported endpoint hardware managed by the Desktop team. Be prepared to travel to other USNH locations when requested to assist with projects or provide additional support. Requirements Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience: Associate’s degree and four years of experience, bachelor’s degree and two years of experience, or combination of education and experience equal to six years.· Expertise in multiple information technology areas (networks, configuration management, security, operating systems, software) and experience with both Windows and Macintosh OSX computer platforms, handheld devices/smartphones, and networking. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Computer hardware replacement/upgrade skills such as memory upgrades, hard drive, system board, battery replacements, etc. Strong customer-focused support skills. Organizational skills and effective oral and written communication skills. Project management, strategic planning, and asset management experience Familiarity with Windows Active Directory and Jamf Pro/Macintosh server technology is desirable. Excellent Customer service experience.  Other Requirements: Valid driver’s license.  Preferred Qualifications: Proven knowledge of/or experience with USNH acceptable computing practices and security policies and procedures is also highly desirable. Experience providing technology support in a higher education environment.   Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Cover Letter Contact Information for 3 Professional References Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration. Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed. This position falls within the collective bargaining unit for the Keene State College Administrative Staff Association (KSCASA), an affiliate of the National Education Association of New Hampshire (NEA-NH). Keene State College is located in the scenic Monadnock region of Southwest New Hampshire and is an affiliate of the University System of New Hampshire. Located approximately 2 hours from Boston or Hartford CT, and 4 hours from New York City, the region contains many opportunities to enjoy outdoor recreation, cultural events, and a strong sense of community. To learn more about Keene State College, the University System of New Hampshire, and the Keene community, please visit: https://www.keene.edu , https://www.usnh.edu/ or https://www.ci.keene.nh.us . EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Compensation Pay Range: $23.01 - $38.03 The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Keene"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Web-Developer_JR7231": {
      "title": "Web Developer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Web Developer will work with a team to develop, maintain and enhance database-driven websites, applications and web elements for the public-facing websites of the University System of New Hampshire and its institutions with a strong focus toward user experience, digital accessibility, SEO principles and client specifications. The Web Developer provides technical leadership to support USNH strategic initiatives.  In this role, you will develop and extend the Drupal content management system framework as well as develop software using PHP, JavaScript, jQuery, HTML, CSS, SQL, and/or other languages. Experience in Web Services (SOAP, REST) and source code control (GitLab) is required. You will also assist in establishing and maintaining a development environment that uses industry best practices for change management. This includes effective use of code repositories, properly leveraging development-test-production environments, and adherence to security protocols and auditable programming standards. Duties/Responsibilities Software Development (80%) Develop websites and other software applications to meet client needs within the scope of the USNH institutions’ web style guides and policies. This includes designing, writing, and implementing new application software and enhancements to existing software; as well as designing application system solutions that employ current and emerging technologies. Build standards-compliant websites using content management systems like Drupal and WordPress, and web technologies like PHP, HTML, React, and CSS. Work with complex data structures within relational databases. Collaborate across teams to integrate AI capabilities into workflows and align AI initiatives with organizational goals. Leverage AI to improve code quality and automate coding tasks. This includes testing, debugging, and improving efficiency by analyzing code for vulnerabilities and suggesting improvements. Troubleshoot issues as required. Maintain technical skills to ensure currency with new and emerging web technologies. Provide documentation and technical support for supported applications. Coordinate the tracking, implementation, and testing of software. Oversee the maintenance schedule for software applications to ensure they stay up-to-date with the latest stable versions and security releases. Manage document libraries, Git and other information warehouses. Client Services (15%) Working closely with other project leaders, this position provides technical leadership by estimating project hours, developing functional and technical specifications, establishing timelines for software projects requested by our customers, and ensuring timely delivery of properly functioning application software. Other (5%) Other duties as assigned. May include training, supervision, professional development, and research. Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience: Bachelor’s degree and six years of experience in information technology field, Master’s and four years, or combination of education and experience equal to ten years. Required   Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Ability to be flexible, adapt and promote organizational core beliefs and values. Demonstrated experience researching, analyzing, and implementing strategies to leverage technology to improve the user experience and/or develop new capabilities to meet emerging opportunities or challenges. Experience in database-driven web applications, HTML5, CSS, JavaScript, React, PHP, Drupal or WordPress content management systems. Working knowledge of at least one SQL-based database. Knowledge of version control systems such as Git or SVN. Strong organizational skills with effective oral and written communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Relational database management experience. Leadership experience. Experience with project management tools and methodologies. Experience working in higher education. Customer service experience. Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Cover Letter Contact Information for 3 Professional References Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration. Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed. The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Compensation Pay Range: $69,560.00 - $124,580.00 The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Business-Advisor_JR7799": {
      "title": "Business Advisor (NH Southern region)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe New Hampshire Small Business Development Center (NH SBDC), an outreach program of the University of New Hampshire, Peter T. Paul College of Business and Economics, is seeking a business advisor for the Southern Region of the state. Under the direction of the Regional Director, evaluate and analyze small business issues and provide solutions-based approaches and recommendations. Work with New Hampshire small businesses across the spectrum of management issues, including finance, marketing, administration, regulatory, etc. Conduct research to stay current on small business issues nationally and in New Hampshire, and bring those lessons to bear in advising. Work with other federal and state programs to increase education, outreach and awareness of environmental issues and programs available to small businesses. Maintain client files in SBDC database, and liaise with Lead Center to fulfill requests for information. Work on other special assignments as needed. Duties/Responsibilities Interview and assess client needs. Provide in-depth, one-on-one confidential business advising and technical assistance to start-up and existing businesses. Determine appropriate educational resources to share. Identify and analyze business issues, develop and implement solutions in a timely manner and conduct research using public and private sources. Assist clients with developing business, financing and marketing plans, as well as a full range of management issues that include personnel issues and understanding the state and regional business climate. Promote growth and sustainability measured through sales increases, job creation and capital formation. Understand network of professionals to which businesses may need to be referred. Administrative work to include: Provide information on client stories. Support Lead Center requests (e.g., surveys, time-sensitive requests). Track, enter and manage client data in MIS and attend SBDC staff events. Identify opportunities to improve service through professional development. Promote the SBDC program and advocate for small businesses through presentations to communities and entities. Support the development of appropriate advertising, promotion and marketing materials. Attend state and regional meetings and conferences as required. Support area, state and federal projects concerning small businesses and disseminate results to community. Build and maintain relationships with community economic development organizations, lending institutions, private sector and other referral partners. Requirements Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience: Bachelor’s in accounting, business management, or related field and 3-5 years of accounting/financial management or related experience. Three to five years of business advising experience. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: One year of operational experience carrying out assignments using management skills. Ability to meet and work with diverse groups of people. Communication skills, both verbal and written. Willingness to travel extensively on short notice and to make overnight stays, if required. Some familiarity with computer programming and data analysis techniques. Small business ownership experience preferred. Experience in a consulting or related service organization working on assignments for external clients. Knowledge of a specialized field of business; such as, accounting, sales, marketing, etc. Preferred Qualifications: MBA preferred. Equivalency by training and experience considered. Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Cover Letter Contact Information for 3 Professional References Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration. Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed. Please be advised that this position is supported by external sponsor funding. As such, continued employment in this role is contingent upon the availability of those external funds. If, for any reason, the sponsor funding is reduced or discontinued, employment may be subject to modification or termination in accordance with applicable policies and procedures.  The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Compensation Pay Range: $52,520.00 - $93,640.00 The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Early-Childhood-Teacher-I_JR9203": {
      "title": "Early Childhood Teacher I",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Early Childhood Teacher I position is part of the UNH Laboratory School within the College of Health and Human Services, Department of Human Development and Family Studies. Reporting to the Executive Director and Assistant Director, the teacher collaborates with classroom staff to plan, implement, and assess high-quality early childhood programs for children, families, and university students. The position may be assigned to infant, toddler, or preschool classrooms based on program needs. Salary Information: Salary decisions take several factors into consideration, including internal equity, budget, and a candidate’s skills and experience. The budgeted salary for this grade 14 position is approximately $19.00 - $20.00 per hour. Duties/Responsibilities: Curriculum and Teaching (60%) Plan, implement, and evaluate developmentally and culturally appropriate learning experiences for children. Observe, assess, and document children's growth and development to inform curriculum planning. Maintain a safe, engaging, and inclusive classroom environment that supports children's learning and well-being. Supervise children during all classroom activities and routines Classroom Leadership and Team Collaboration (30%) Build positive partnerships with families through regular communication, conferences, and family engagement activities. Collaborate with teaching team members to ensure effective classroom operations, shared decision-making, and high-quality programming. Supervise and mentor student interns, teaching assistants, and practicum students as assigned. Program Operations, Documentation, and Professional Leadership (10%) Maintain required child, family, assessment, and classroom records in compliance with licensing, accreditation, and program standards. Participate in staff meetings, professional development, committees, and center-wide initiatives. Support research, advocacy, and continuous program improvement efforts. Perform classroom operational duties and contribute to the health, safety, and maintenance of the program. Requirements: Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience Bachelor's degree in Early Childhood Education, Preschool Education, or Elementary Education (including at least six credits in Early Childhood/Preschool Education) and four (4) years of related teaching experience. Required Licenses & Certifications New Hampshire Early Childhood Professional Development Credential for Early Childhood Educator. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Strong knowledge of child development and developmentally appropriate practices for infants, toddlers, and preschool-aged children. Ability to plan, implement, assess, and adapt curriculum based on children's interests, strengths, and developmental needs. Excellent communication and relationship-building skills with children, families, colleagues, and university students. Effective leadership, collaboration, and mentoring skills, including the ability to supervise interns and teaching assistants. Strong organizational, documentation, and record-keeping skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines. Ability to lift up to 50 pounds and perform the physical requirements of an early childhood classroom Preferred Qualifications: Current Pediatric CPR and First Aid certification. Experience in a NAEYC-accredited program, laboratory school setting, or supervising student teachers/interns preferred. Applicant Instructions:    Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the   My Experience: Resume/CV   section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents)   Resume/CV   Cover Letter   Contact Information for 3 Professional References   Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration. Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed. The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Compensation Pay Range: $40,020.00 - $71,130.00 The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham"
    },
