    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Postdoctoral-Research-Associate_JR9363": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app Applications are invited for a Postdoctoral Research Associate position in Prof. Mrityunjay Kothari’s group. The focus of the position is to advance the theoretical and computational mechanics of soft solids under coupled physical environments. The position is situated within a sponsored research program on the finite-deformation mechanics of soft and biological materials, where the central questions concern how large elastic deformation couples to additional fields—thermal, transport, phase-change, and damage—within a rigorous continuum framework. The researcher will develop continuum theories and the corresponding finite-element implementations that resolve these couplings, translate constitutive theory into verified numerical code, and publish results in leading mechanics journals. Beyond core research, the position offers opportunities to develop collaborations, to gain structured experience in research-proposal writing, and to mentor graduate and undergraduate students, preparing the candidate for an independent research career. This is a full-time, benefits-eligible appointment, renewable contingent on performance and continued funding, and is not considered essential staff. The position is for one year initially, with renewal contingent on performance. Duties/Responsibilities The primary duties of the position are to conduct research on the mechanics of soft solids and to develop the associated theoretical and computational tools. Specific responsibilities include: formulating theories and experiments, computational models and their implementation (such as in FEniCS/FEniCSx and in Abaqus via user-element and user-material subroutines (UEL/UMAT)), preparing manuscripts for peer-reviewed journals and presenting results at conferences. The researcher will also gain experience contributing to research proposals and technical reports for the sponsoring program, and will help mentor graduate and undergraduate students on theory, code, and experiment development. Requirements Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience: Doctoral degree in Mechanical Engineering, Applied Mechanics, or Solid Mechanics completed by the start date. Strong track record of high-quality publications in peer-reviewed journals; demonstrated research expertise in nonlinear (finite-strain) continuum mechanics and the mechanics of solids. Demonstrated proficiency in finite-element implementation through at least one of FEniCS/FEniCSx or Abaqus user subroutines (UEL/UMAT) in Fortran, together with scientific programming in Python. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Strong command of solid mechanics, especially in finite deformation and coupled continuum theories. Proven ability to translate continuum theory into verified finite-element code, including implementing custom elements and material models. Strong written and oral scientific communication, evidenced by first-author publications and conference presentations. Ability to work independently, manage research milestones, and collaborate within a multi-investigator project.  Other Requirements: U.S. work authorization at the time of appointment; the candidate must be eligible to work on federally funded research.   Preferred Qualifications: Candidate should have a PhD in Solid Mechanics specialization. Experience with nonlinear elasticity, finite deformation mechanics, continuum mechanics, finite element implementation in FEniCS/FEniCSx/ABAQUS UEL,UMAT. Strong publication record in mechanics, materials, applied mathematics, or related journals. Proficiency with HPC, parallel solvers (PETSc), and version control (Git).  Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Cover Letter Contact Information for 3 Professional References Additionally, upload the following documents within the Application Questions section of the application: Research Statement Three representative publications with your contributions clearly identified Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration. Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed. Compensation Pay Range: $ 60K annually The rank of the selected candidate will depend upon the candidate’s qualifications. Please be advised that this position is partly supported by external sponsor funding. As such, continued employment in this role is contingent upon the availability of those external funds. If, for any reason, the sponsor funding is reduced or discontinued, employment may be subject to modification or termination in accordance with applicable policies and procedures. The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham Salary Grade: Faculty 01"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Plymouth-State-University/Program-Support-Assistant_JR9380": {
      "title": "Program Support Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app Internal Candidate Identified The Holmes Center for School Partnerships and Educator Preparation is recruiting a non-benefited, part- time University Supervisor for the Teacher Education programs. Duties/Responsibilities Coach and evaluate teacher candidates in the classroom Education programs include: Art, Elementary Ed, English, Health, Music, Physical Education, Social Studies, and Special Education Minimum Qualifications Must be qualified, skilled practitioner familiar with state and national standards Able to make a part- time commitment  Requires travel to K-12 schools Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Compensation Pay Range: $50 per hour Plymouth State University offers high-quality baccalaureate, graduate, and doctoral degree programs. Through research and innovative community partnerships, the University contributes to the economic, social, cultural, and environmental development of the North Country and Lakes Region of New Hampshire and beyond. Plymouth State University (PSU) is transforming the campus to create a first-of-its-kind university holistically organized around integrated clusters. Our goal is to provide a dynamic interdisciplinary and innovative learning environment. Students, faculty, staff, and community will connect to solve real-world challenges that will benefit people and organizations at all levels. We are a residential and comprehensive university with a warm and engaged learning community focused on teaching excellence and regional engagement. The University is located in the heart of the Lakes Region and White Mountains of New Hampshire and serves approximately 4,300 undergraduate and more than 2,000 graduate students. Surrounded by lakes and mountains, PSU’s 170-acre campus provides students with an outstanding natural laboratory for learning and an ideal setting for outdoor recreation. PSU has consistently earned national recognition for its commitment to community service, environmental sustainability, academic excellence, and employee wellness. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Salary Grade: Adjunct Hourly Staff 00 Location: Plymouth"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Adjunct-Research-Support_JR9397": {
      "title": "Adjunct Research Support",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app The University of New Hampshire Prevention Innovations Research Center (PIRC) Research Assistant (RA) will assist with externally and internally funded research projects. The RA position involves assisting the research team with recruiting research participants, facilitating focus groups and key stakeholder interviews, developing and implementing research surveys, analyzing both quantitative and qualitative data, and writing scholarly and practitioner articles. Duties/Responsibilities Preparing resources and materials for research activities. Collecting data (e.g., surveys, interviews and focus groups). Analyzing quantitative and qualitative results. Requirements Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience: Some research experience, either through a social science or public health research methods course or practical experience in a research laboratory. Students majoring in psychology, sociology, public health, or a health-related field. Must be dedicated to PIRC's mission of ending interpersonal violence. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Research experience in both qualitative and quantitative methods, including the use of survey software (e.g., Qualtrics) and analysis software (e.g., SPSS, STATA, Atlas.ti). Ability to work independently and accurately, and to problem-solve technical and methodological issues that arise during research.  Knowledge of the ethical considerations surrounding research on sensitive topics and the submission of Institutional Review Board (IRB) applications.  Requires strong organization and interpersonal skills, as well as the ability to work as part of a team. Professional oral/written communication skills are required. Proficiency with the Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, SharePoint, OneDrive) and CANVA. Foundational knowledge of violence prevention Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Compensation Pay Range: $15-18 per hour Please be advised that this position is supported by external sponsor funding. As such, continued employment in this role is contingent upon the availability of those external funds. If, for any reason, the sponsor funding is reduced or discontinued, employment may be subject to modification or termination in accordance with applicable policies and procedures.  The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham Salary Grade: Adjunct Hourly Staff 00"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Assistant-Director-of-Operations--and-Director-of-On-Campus-Recruiting_JR9310": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Operations, and Director of On Campus Recruiting",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app The Assistant Director of Football Operations / Director of On-Campus Recruiting manages the logistics of recruiting and team operations so coaches can focus on coaching rather than administrative work. Core responsibilities include coordinating official and unofficial campus visits, maintaining the recruiting database and prospect communication pipeline, and serving as the primary point of contact for prospects and high school coaches,  a role especially valuable as we build out our NH high school coach relationship network. Beyond recruiting, this position handles team travel logistics, camp registration and event coordination (Prospect Camp, Youth Camps, Jr. Days), and tracking NCAA/CAA compliance related to recruiting activity. In short, it’s the connective tissue between recruiting strategy and its execution on the ground, ensuring every prospect visit, camp, and recruiting touchpoint runs smoothly and leaves a strong impression of the program. Duties/Responsibilities Team Operations (40%) Manage team travel logistics for away games (transportation, lodging, meals) Support practice and meeting scheduling Assist with day-to-day administrative needs of the football program Recruiting Operations (40%) Coordinate and execute official and unofficial campus visits (scheduling, logistics, hosting, itineraries) Maintain the recruiting database and manage prospect communication workflows Serve as primary point of contact for prospects and their families throughout the recruiting process Support development of the NH high school coach relationship network Camps & Events (20%) Handle registration and logistics for Prospect Camp, Youth Camps, Recruit Jr. Days Coordinate staffing and volunteer support for camp days Requirements Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution required Minimum of two (2) years of experience working within a college or professional football program, in operations, recruiting, administrative, or operational capacities Required Licenses & Certifications: Valid Drivers License Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Working knowledge of NCAA and conference recruiting rules and compliance requirements Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines simultaneously Excellent written and verbal communication skills Ability to build and maintain relationships with prospects, families, and high school coaches Proficiency with recruiting database/CRM software (e.g., Arms, Teamworks) Ability to work effectively under pressure during high-volume recruiting periods Strong attention to detail, particularly with compliance documentation Ability to work evenings, weekends, and holidays as dictated by the recruiting and competitive calendar Team-oriented mindset with the ability to collaborate across departments (admissions, compliance, registrar) Discretion in handling sensitive and confidential information related to prospective student-athletes Other Requirements: Ability to travel as needed for team travel purposes Successful completion of a background check Compliance with all University, CAA, and NCAA policies and regulations Willingness to work a flexible schedule, including irregular hours during peak recruiting and camp seasons. Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Compensation Pay Range: $15 / hour The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham Salary Grade: Adjunct Hourly Staff 00"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Program-Compliance-and-Data-Manager_JR9385": {
      "title": "Program Compliance and Data Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Program Compliance and Data Manager works with the Education Department Chair, Program Coordinators and Directors, and individual course Instructors to oversee the ongoing and periodic review processes of accreditation and compliance for the University’s educator preparation licensure programs primarily and non-licensure programs secondarily. The position involves data collection, analysis, and reporting that supports compliance across all UNH educator preparation programs, university wide. Core responsibilities include preparing for state, regional, and national accreditation processes and reviews; organizing and coordinating all surveys and graduate placement data for the Department; advising educator preparation students of licensure requirements and pathways in “pre-advising”; and preparing and providing appropriate student and program data to the Director of Educator Preparation, the Chair of the Education Department, UNH and USNH leadership offices, and appropriate public stakeholders for varied reporting requirements. The position requires a high degree of independent judgment, strong data-management and systems expertise, and the ability to coordinate across departments, colleges, and external agencies such as the New Hampshire Education Department. This position is not considered essential staff (i.e., it is not required to report to work during curtailment). Duties/Responsibilities Data Management: Compliance (30%) Maintain Professional Education Standards matrices (ED 500s and ED 600s). Maintain PEPP (Programs Approved for Educator Preparation) advising worksheets. Manage candidate- and course-based assessment systems (e.g., Canvas Outcomes): Set up assessment sites, field questions from instructors and students about candidate- and course-based assessment systems, and maintain repositories of candidate work for 5+ years. Serve as the primary contact for instructors on program/candidate assessment tools and databases; assist faculty with designing assessments, rubrics, and reporting structures in databases. Coordinate communication between course leads and adjuncts for all courses, and support syllabus compliance for all Education Department and educator preparation (UNH-wide) courses. When databases or state/university requirements change, research and recommend new tools or functions to the Director of Educator Preparation and the Chair; attend database trainings and serve as the contact person liaising with vendors and UNH IT on compliance needs and database products. Manage program assessment systems, including year-end Qualtrics surveys of interns/student teachers, recent graduates, clinical educators, and hiring principals; distribute surveys, track response rates, and prepare reports for the Director of Educator Preparation and curriculum advisory committees. Collect post-graduation employment and graduate placement data. Data Management: Candidates (25%) Run Webi/Workday reports of students enrolled in undergraduate majors associated with a PEPP (i.e., a licensure pathway); confirm with program coordinators the list of students anticipated to apply to a PEPP. Support administrative tasks in GradLeaders; respond to questions from students, advisors, and program coordinators regarding GradLeaders; and assist the Clinical Coordinator, as needed, with GradLeaders tasks. Prepare audits of student records, including documentation of transfer credits, for degree completion, obtaining advisor sign-off. Prepare audits of student records, including documentation of successful completion of culminating assessments, for licensure completion, obtaining licensure officer sign-off. Accreditation Support (25%, increases prior to accreditation visits) Prepare for state and national accreditation visits in conjunction with the Department Chair, Director of Educator Preparation, and appropriate faculty: participate in reviewer training; establish timelines; schedule meetings for faculty, staff, and the Steering Committee leading up to the visit; create the onsite visit agenda; coordinate reviewer reimbursements, hotels, and meals; support Exhibit Room design; collect and organize student and program data with the Director; and manage documents provided by departments for the Exhibit Room. Support self-study preparation and any rejoinders, collecting and organizing student and program data to demonstrate standards compliance. Write and submit the NHED Annual Report. Write and submit the Title II Report. Information Dissemination & Other (20%) Communicate changes in standards and administrative rules to departments and colleges with PEPPs. Communicate updates and changes in standards and administrative rules affecting application and entrance processes to college and school admissions teams. Field student questions regarding licensure and assist with responses to common licensure questions, as directed by the Licensure Officer. Maintain websites, SharePoint sites, and flyers regarding licensure requirements (BASA, licensure testing). Support data collection and reporting for external college surveys, such as U.S. News & World Report. Coordinate information sessions, advising sessions, and orientations at various program checkpoints; advise prospective students. Collect, process, and track clinical educator tuition waiver requests. Participate in department, college, and university committees that support the work of accreditation and licensure. Depending on candidate qualifications/interest and Departmental need, the position may involve opportunities to teach courses at the undergraduate or graduate level. Requirements Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience: Bachelor's degree in Education or a related field Experience supervising pre-service or practicing teachers Experience with technology such as database and website management and Workday/Webi reporting.   Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Collaborative interpersonal skills to work both within and outside the University. Formal training and current knowledge of educational practice and assessment. Strong data-management, database, and systems skills, including assessment-management platforms (e.g., Watermark Taskstream / Student Learning & Licensure, Canvas Outcomes) and reporting tools (Webi/Workday). Ability to interpret and apply state, regional, and national accreditation and licensure standards and administrative rules. Strong attention to detail and accuracy in auditing student records and managing compliance data. Effective written and verbal communication skills, including preparing reports for institutional and external stakeholders. Ability to manage multiple deadlines and coordinate across departments, colleges, and external agencies such as the NH Education Department.   Preferred Qualifications: Advanced degree in Education (e.g., M.Ed., Ed.S., CAGS, Ph.D.) or a related field. Experience in educator preparation, accreditation, or program compliance in a higher education setting. Familiarity with New Hampshire Education Department licensure requirements and PEPP processes. Experience preparing state or national accreditation self-studies and reports (e.g., NHED Annual Report, Title II). Experience with GradLeaders or a comparable student life-cycle/placement system.   Applicant Instructions:    Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the   My Experience: Resume/CV   section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents)   Resume/CV   Cover Letter   Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration. Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed.    The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Compensation Pay Range: $45,790.00 - $81,530.00 The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Academic-Year-Gym-Clinic-AT_JR9387": {
      "title": "Academic Year Gym Clinic AT",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app The University of New Hampshire is seeking a Fully Certified Athletic Trainer for to assist Gymnasts during the Fall Clinic. Duties/Responsibilities Present to assist in any needs during clinics Treats in-clinic injuries Designs rehabilitation programs Informs injured players’ families of athletes’ condition Monitors progress Maintains records Plans preventive measures Requirements Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience: Fully certified Athletic Trainer with a bachelor's or master degree. Must have some understanding of the sport of gymnastics. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Knowledge and understanding of gymnastics and the physical demands of the sport. Familiarity with common gymnastics injuries and appropriate injury prevention, evaluation, and management techniques. Knowledge of and ability to apply various athletic taping and wrapping techniques. Ability to recognize signs and symptoms of injury and determine when an athlete should be removed from participation or referred for further evaluation. Ability to provide appropriate first aid and emergency care when needed. Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced gymnastics environment with athletes of varying ages and skill levels. Strong communication and interpersonal skills when working with athletes, coaches, parents/guardians, and other medical personnel. Ability to maintain accurate and timely injury and treatment documentation. Ability to remain calm and make sound decisions in emergency or high-pressure situations. Understanding of appropriate safety practices and injury-prevention strategies specific to gymnastics training. Ability to work collaboratively with gymnastics coaches and clinic staff to support athlete health and safety. Current CPR/AED and First Aid certification preferred/required, as applicable. Ability to communicate appropriately and professionally with children and adolescents. Understanding of the additional considerations involved in providing care to minors, including appropriate boundaries, supervision, and communication with parents/guardians. Other Requirements: Ability to work scheduled gymnastics clinic hours, including evenings and/or weekends as needed. Ability to remain on-site and available throughout assigned clinic sessions. Ability to respond quickly to injuries or medical emergencies during clinic activities. Successful completion of any required University or department background screening and onboarding requirements. Compliance with all University, athletic training, youth program, and gymnastics clinic policies and procedures. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience providing athletic training or sports medicine services in a gymnastics or similar acrobatic sport setting. Experience working with youth and adolescent athletes. Familiarity with common gymnastics injuries, injury prevention, and rehabilitation techniques. Experience with a variety of athletic taping and wrapping techniques. Experience working in a fast-paced sports or clinical environment. Strong communication skills and the ability to work collaboratively with coaches, athletes, parents/guardians, and other medical professionals. Experience providing medical coverage for camps, clinics, practices, or competitions. Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Cover Letter Contact Information for 3 Professional References Compensation Pay Range: $45 an hour Approx: 6-8 hours of work The University of New Hampshire is committed to providing a safe environment for all persons, including but not limited to children, and to prevent and respond to abuse, neglect and crimes against children. All UNH youth program staff shall be subject to a criminal background check as required by NH State Law. Staff and volunteers will also be required to complete periodic child safety training. The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham Salary Grade: Adjunct Hourly Staff 00"
    },
