    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Administrative-Assistant---Paul-College_JR9373": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant - Paul College",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app Under the broad supervision of the Team Lead of the Paul Administrative Support Services (PASS) Team, and working in close coordination with the PASS Team, this part-time Administrative Assistant III is assigned to support one or more academic departments within Paul College. The incumbent works closely with department chairs, faculty, and other units to provide diverse administrative and operational support. The position works independently within established procedures and exercises judgment and problem-solving skills in carrying out day-to-day administrative activities and supporting the execution and logistics of academic departments at Paul College. Additional responsibilities may include assisting with the promotion of department events and activities through print and digital channels; supporting routine purchasing, travel, and expense processes; preparing materials as needed for courses, correspondence, and meetings; assisting with department committee, meeting, and event scheduling; responding to requests for information related to department programs and activities; supporting travel arrangements; attending meetings and recording proceedings; applying departmental and University guidelines, policies, and procedures; and handling confidential materials with discretion. As a member of the PASS Team, this position contributes to a collaborative, shared-services model of administrative support across Paul College academic departments and may be called upon to provide coverage or assistance to other departments within the PASS Team structure as operational needs and priorities change. This is a part-time, adjunct (non-benefited) position at 0.5 FTE (20 hours per week) based on campus at Paul College in Durham, New Hampshire. The regular work schedule is Monday through Friday, 7:30 a.m.–12:00 p.m., inclusive of a required 30-minute unpaid break each day while classes are in session, with flexibility during non-class weeks (Winter/Spring break, Summer, etc.). The position is expected to work on campus five days per week to support the operational and coverage needs of the College. Some flexibility in scheduled hours may occasionally be required to support department or College events and other operational needs. This position is contingent upon the availability of funding each fiscal cycle. Continuation of the role is subject to annual review and budget approval. This position is not eligible for institutional benefits. Duties/Responsibilities: Department Operations Support (50%) Serve as a primary point of contact for internal and external inquiries from departments, students, parents, alumni, and partner organizations; coordinate academic program details, identify and resolve problems, and provide specialized program information via phone and email. Create and initiate written correspondence in accordance with professional business and academic standards. Coordinate schedules for academic and departmental meetings, lectures, events, and conferences involving faculty, staff, industry professionals, alumni, and students; reserve space and oversee telecommunication needs; arrange and manage virtual meetings (e.g. Teams or equivalent platforms); participate in and record meeting proceedings as requested; prepare, format, and distribute agendas and minutes in a detailed, professional format. Coordinate with other PASS Team administrative staff to ensure adequate coverage across departments during vacations, sick days, and other absences. Collaborate with relevant campus offices (e.g. Career Services, Dean's Office) as requested. Maintain existing secure online file-sharing, storage, and collaboration platform for department and faculty files, shared in coordination with faculty, staff, and other offices as appropriate. Assist faculty with proctoring arrangements and exam scheduling, including coordinating with testing/accessibility services for students with academic accommodations; reserve rooms for makeup exams and arrange for classroom proctors as requested. Support faculty recruitment efforts by coordinating departmental faculty schedules for candidate interview itineraries and assisting with the organization and management of candidate visits in coordination with the Dean's Office. Project and Events Support (30%) Provide a wide array of complex program support and technical and administrative assistance related to the coordination, planning, organizing, and management of department-level events, which may include symposiums, conferences, faculty presentations, competitions, open houses, admitted student days, and student club activities. Design, create, and produce publications and event collateral including, but not limited to: presentations, event flow documents, timelines, programs, promotional materials, brochures, flyers, posters, invitations, correspondence, print and digital signage, and website content; coordinate appropriate outreach and marketing activities as assigned. Support event logistics including: researching and securing event venues and rooms; creating promotional content; assisting with event publicity efforts; arranging technical support and catering; maintaining related supplies and equipment; monitoring participant registrations and tracking attendees; printing name-tags and other event materials; ; supporting guest as needed; providing program information to participants and speakers; and other related supportive day of execution needs. Financial Support (10%) Exercising discretion and sound judgment, monitor department spending via established processes that support department funded programs, projects, meetings, events, clubs, and activities; secure all necessary approvals prior to purchases; review expenses for appropriateness; verify supporting documentation for accuracy. Support travel and expense reimbursements for faculty, students, speakers, and guests; provide guidance on PCard usage and reimbursement requests; verify supporting documentation. Departmental Data Management and other duties as assigned (10%) Create and provide periodic statistical, enrollment, and progress reports using professional business and academic standards. Work closely with assigned department chair(s) to monitor academic course schedules; maintain databases; perform data entry and retrieval; create spreadsheets and reports; and compile enrollment reports. Ensure accuracy of student records and departmental data; adhere to all applicable legal requirements and regulations, including FERPA; maintain confidentiality and discretion when using and conveying sensitive or confidential information. Support faculty in tracking, coordinating, and organizing outside engagement information for department-sponsored events to support accreditation and assessment processes as applicable. Requirements: Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience: Associate's degree or equivalent combination of education and experience. Minimum of 3 years of progressively responsible administrative or office support experience. Demonstrated proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook) and virtual meeting platforms (e.g. Teams). Strong written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities, work independently, and exercise sound judgment. Experience handling confidential information with discretion and in compliance with applicable regulations (e.g., FERPA). Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Business Administration, Communications, or a related field. Experience in a higher education or academic department setting. Experience with event planning and coordination. Familiarity with budget monitoring and expense reporting processes. Experience with digital content creation and/or graphic design tools (e.g., Canva, Adobe Suite). Experience with web content management systems. Experience with Workday ERP platform Applicant Instructions:    Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the   My Experience: Resume/CV   section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents)   Resume/CV   Cover Letter   Contact Information for 3 Professional References    ​   Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration. Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed.    Compensation Pay Range:   $20.00-$21.00 per hour The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham Salary Grade: Adjunct Hourly Staff 00"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Cloud-Operations-Technical-Lead_JR9192": {
      "title": "Cloud Operations Team Lead",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe Cloud Operations Team Lead is responsible for leading the team charged with building, supporting, and maintaining the E nterprise IT automation toolkit, supporting services, and other processes used within our CI/CD , DevOps , and Infrastructure as Code managed environments. The responsibilities of the cloud operations team is to support the management, configuration, and system and service lifecycle of all virtual machines, containerized environments, cloud compute and storage, all database environments , and support for business AI, business intelligence, and data engineering services. These tools also support the software development operations across several additional departments. The position reports directly to the Cloud Operations and Engineering group manager, which is part of the Enterprise IT Infrastructure service line.   Job Description   Team Lead   Provide supervision to a team of 3 Automation and Platform Services team staff   O versee all work done by the team including being accountable for quality and timeliness of delivery   Plan and schedule the team resources   Perform hiring and staff onboarding   Support staff professional development and training   Conduct formalized annual reviews as well as ongoing performance reviews and goal settings with staff   Motivate staff to meet goals set by strategic initiatives as well as normal workload   Insure employees are adhering to institutional policies, taking appropriate action, verbal and written to improve employee performance   Provide input into merit-based salary adjustments,      Automation services    Develop and administer the automation and platform services environments hosting mission critical, high availability enterprise applications and web hosting· Configuration management and workflow   Develop and maintain procedures for system management and software deployment tasks as well as providing input into implementing continuous improvement of such practices and processes   Consult with developers, application , and system administrators in planning needs   Develop automation for system and application maintenance, configuration, performance monitoring, and security testing   Document all processes, procedures, and services   Maintain system monitoring of performance, availability, and scalability     Platform Services   Provide integration services for private and public cloud hosting platforms.   Provide support for issues that arise with hosting, application hosting, and server applications   Develop DevOps, CI/CD, and Configuration Management processes   Develop and service deployment pipelines, in collaboration with development staff, application Administration staff, system administration staff   Follow all established incident and problem management practices. Continuous Improvement   Research and technically assess new web application , development operations, and continuous integration technologies for service development, support, and process improvement.,       General Support   Provide morning, evening, and weekend coverage for time critical events, addressing production issues, or other changes. Oversee staffing, resource planning, performance, professional development, and policy compliance, while ensuring high-quality, timely delivery aligned with strategic priorities. Other duties as assigned.   Minimum Requir e ments     Bachelor’s degree and two years of experience in information technology field, Associate’s and four years, or combination of education and experience equal to six years Linux/Apache/MySQL/PHP (LAMP) system administration Apache Tomcat or similar experience   Familiarity working in VMware virtualization environments, Azure, AWS , and other relevant public cloud hosting environment Scripting with common script and development languages (Python, PHP, Bash, PowerShell, etc.)   Application/System performance tuning, troubleshooting and monitoring   Ability to learn and adapt to new technologies on a near constant basis· Development Operations (DevOps) experience   Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) experience   Experience with container orchestration (Docker, Docker Engine, Kubernetes, etc. )   Experience with configuration management tools (Salt, Puppet, Systems Center Configuration Manager)   Experience with Application Programing Interface (API)  Experience, exposure, or knowledge of Site Reliability Engineering and its practices   Documentation and knowledge sharing abilities     Preferred Qualifications     Understanding of Drupal CMS development (internals, themes, modules etc ) Understanding of TCP/IP Networking, Virtualization (VMWare) and system hardware.   Understanding of other database systems (Oracle, SQL Server)   Knowledge of system and application security threats and countermeasures Knowledge of authentication and authorization via LDAP or Active Directory Familiarity with ITIL/IT Service Management practices   Customer focused and able to present a positive outlook within the team and to end customers   Highly self-motivated yet works well within a team   Highly accountable and works well within a project-driven organization   Result and detail-oriented and ability to work simultaneously on multiple projects     Applicant Instructions:    Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the   My Experience: Resume/CV   section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents)   Resume/CV   Cover Letter   Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration. Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed.    The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Compensation Pay Range: $69,560.00 - $124,580.00 The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Health-Science-Simulation-Technician-II_JR9336": {
      "title": "Health Science Simulation Technician II",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app Under the direction of the nursing faculty, this position performs duties in the Health Sciences Simulation Center (HSSC) to support faculty in providing quality simulated learning experiences for students. Duties/Responsibilities Boot up and shut down simulators, prepare and break down task trainers, simulation rooms and other equipment/props for simulation or skills lab sessions  Operate a variety of computers and technical simulation equipment pertaining to simulation scenarios, including virtual reality software and equipment Control simulator software to model simulator’s physiological response to instructor and/or scenario specifications Operate and maintains audio-visual and debriefing systems during simulations Reset rooms in between sessions (restock, replenish supplies as needed)  Maintain current knowledge of simulation/lab equipment and operation manuals Clean equipment as needed (manikin, task trainers)  Assist in development, and demonstration of instructional best practices for the use of the manikins and equipment to help elevate the simulation experiences of students and faculty Provide technical support for task trainers and multimedia peripherals, including: Vital sign monitors IV pumps and feeding pumps Beds/examination tables, headwalls, patient monitors, and other healthcare equipment Provide theatrical production (costuming and moulage) for simulation scenarios as requested Provide technical assistance and support to students, faculty, and staff in the use of simulation and skills lab equipment and software Enforce the safety and security of the simulation and skills labs according to established procedures, policies, and laws Ensure that simulation and skills laboratories and other assigned areas are maintained in a clean, safe and orderly condition Work with students during their sessions in HSSC Facilitate simulation-based experiences and activities in collaboration with nursing faculty Assist with laboratory needs including setup and cleanup for lab learning activities, manage lab supplies and provide overall student and faculty lab support  Collaborate with nursing faculty to provide consistent and relevant student learning experiences to meet the course objectives Performs other duties as assigned Requirements Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience : Bachelor’s Degree in Nursing Organizational skills and the ability to follow directions Demonstrated interest, ability and/or experience promoting cultural competency, universal accessibility, and/or diversity Strong problem solving and critical thinking skills Flexible and able to adapt to a dynamic environment based on changing policies, procedures and clinical needs Able to balance multiple tasks simultaneously Required Licenses & Certifications : Unencumbered RN license Knowledge Skills & Abilities : Understanding of nursing concepts and procedures Effective communication and teamwork with faculty, staff, and students Ability to provide constructive feedback during simulations. Adaptability to respond to unexpected changes in simulation scenarios Willingness to learn new technologies and methods Preferred Qualifications : 1-2 years of simulation experience, working with simulation in an educational institution or equivalent setting Certified Healthcare Simulation Operations Specialist (CHSOS) or Certified Healthcare Simulation Educator (CHSE) Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Compensation Pay Range: $28-$35/hour The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham Salary Grade: Adjunct Hourly Staff 00"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Digital-Marketing-Specialist_JR9165": {
      "title": "Digital Marketing Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe digital marketing specialist is responsible for the coordination and execution of UNH's digital workﬂows across UNH’s owned and paid channels. Under the supervision and direction of marketing staff, the digital marketing specialist partners with internal creative, project management, web production, as well as external advertising agencies and platform vendors to ensure digital assets are produced, reviewed, and delivered accurately and on schedule. The digital marketing specialist will also support the day-to-day management of paid media campaigns, including trafficking creative to ad platforms, monitoring campaign performance, and maintaining consistent tracking and UTM conventions across digital properties. This person will work with our internal web and content teams to coordinate asset handoffs to the UNH.edu website, and with our agency partners to ensure campaigns launch on time, on spec, and in alignment with approved media plans. Daily Tasks/Responsibilities:  Work in partnership with project management team maintain/create organize project tracking in Basecamp for digital projects and programs. Serve as the primary monitor for timelines, meeting schedules and communication ﬂows for digital projects Serve as a central point of contact for workﬂow-related questions from internal team members and external vendors for digital projects and programs. Serve as the primary digital asset traffic manager coordinating deliverables like digital ad assets or website copy updates between content creator, stakeholder and producer. Serve as day-to-day partner with digital agency in management of paid digital campaigns, including search, display, and social advertising, across platforms such as Google Ads, Meta, and LinkedIn. Monitor campaign pacing, budgets, and performance against established KPIs, and escalate issues as appropriate. Coordinate with agency vendors on campaign execution, asset delivery, and reporting timelines. Pull and compile routine performance reports from Google Analytics (GA4), Looker studio, and platform-native dashboards on a regular cadence. Maintain UTM parameter governance across campaigns, ensuring consistent tracking conventions are applied to all outbound links and paid placements. Flag performance trends or anomalies and surface them to the digital strategy team with relevant context. Required Qualiﬁcations Bachelor’s degree in marketing, communications, advertising, digital media, or a related ﬁeld. Minimum of 1-3 years of marketing experience. Prior experience or internship in an advertising agency, media company, or in-house digital marketing team Strong understanding of pay-per-click advertising tools and campaign management, including basic understanding of campaign structure, creative specs, and trafficking workﬂows. Working knowledge of Google Analytics (GA4); ability to navigate the platform and interpret standard performance metrics. Google Analytic certiﬁcation is a plus. Strong attention to detail, particularly in reviewing creative assets for spec compliance and QA-ing live campaigns. Clear, professional written communication skills; comfortable corresponding directly with external agency contacts. Ability to manage multiple active projects and deadlines without losing track of details. Familiarity with a web content systems (CMS) like Drupal Applicant Instructions Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/Cover Letter section of your application: Resume/CV Cover Letter Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration.  Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed. Please note t hat salary decisions take several factors into consideration, including internal equity, budget, and a candidate’s skills and experience. The budgeted salary for this position is in the low- to mid- $50k range. The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Compensation Pay Range: $47,920.00 - $85,410.00 The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/UNH-Library-Processing-Archivist--Contract-Librarian_JR9212": {
      "title": "UNH Library Processing Archivist, Contract Librarian",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app The University of New Hampshire (UNH) Library invites applications for a three-year contract librarian position with possibility for renewal as a Processing Archivist at a nationally recognized R1 public research university. This position will arrange, describe, and preserve archival collections to support their long-term accessibility for researchers, students, and the broader scholarly community. Early-career professionals are encouraged to apply. The Processing Archivist will work collaboratively with colleagues in Special Collections and Archives to process incoming and backlog collections, create finding aids and other descriptive records, and contribute to collection management, reference, instruction, acquisition, and appraisal activities as needed. UNH offers a collaborative and welcoming environment, with the opportunity to make a meaningful impact on an academic research library’s collections with statewide significance and national reach. Job Description Summary: The Processing Archivist is responsible for arranging, describing, and preserving archival collections to ensure long-term accessibility for researchers, students, and the broader scholarly community of New Hampshire and beyond. This role assesses incoming materials, establishes intellectual and physical control, and creates clear, comprehensive finding aids in accordance with professional archival standards and best practices. This role provides faculty support for reference, instruction, acquisition, and appraisal activities as needed. Early career professionals are encouraged to apply to this position. Key Responsibilities: Collection Processing Survey, appraise, and prioritize incoming and backlog archival collections with guidance from the Special Collections Librarian and University Archivist. Arrange archival materials following professional archival principles (respect des fonds, original order, provenance). Rehouse materials into appropriate archival storage to ensure long-term preservation. Identify preservation concerns and collaborate with preservation staff as needed.  Description and Metadata Create detailed finding aids, catalog records, and inventories using standards such as DACS , EAD , MARC , or local metadata schemas. Apply controlled vocabularies and authority records (e.g., LCSH, LCAH, AAT, SNAC).  Collection Management Track and manage the progress of processing projects. Recommend processing levels (minimal, baseline, full) based on collection significance, condition, and researcher needs in coordination with the University Archivist and Special Collections Librarian. Contribute to collection management workflows and documentation. Provide support for acquisition and appraisal activities as requested or assigned.  Collaboration & Support Work closely with staff to support the Archives Processing and Access Program. Participate in cross-departmental projects. As needed, provide frontline reference and Reading Room support and back-up for the Public Services Coordinator. Provide instruction support, such as proctoring Reading Room, as needed. As required and if opportunity arises, present and share with library faculty and staff about processing projects. Engage in library, university, and professional service in alignment with position responsibilities that are relevant to their appointment. Contribute to library and university shared governance. Required Qualifications Master’s degree in Library and Information Science from an ALA accredited program with a concentration in archives. 1 year of processing experience working on large collections, demonstrating familiarity with processing archival or manuscript collections (such as an internship, employment, volunteer work, etc.) Familiarity with archival standards (DACS, EAD, MARC) and archival management systems. Knowledge of preservation principles for paper and photographic materials. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment. Preferred Qualifications Experience using archival management platforms such as ArchivesSpace. Familiarity with processing congressional and/or political papers. Familiarity with MPLP processing practices. Knowledge of inclusive description practices. Project management skills and experience establishing workflows. Knowledge of copyright, privacy, and rights-management issues in archives. This position may involve handling fragile materials, lifting archival boxes (up to ~40 lbs), and working in collection storage environments.  Applicant Instructions:    Applications received by 5 pm (EST) on September 8, 2026 will receive priority review. Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the  My Experience: Resume/CV  section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents)   Resume/CV   Cover Letter   Sample finding aid that represents their experience with archival processing Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration. Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed.    Compensation Pay Range:   $75,000 to $86,000  The rank of the selected candidate will depend upon the candidate’s qualifications.   The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham Salary Grade: Librarians 01"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Keene-State-College/Advance-Technician_JR9293": {
      "title": "Advance Technician",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app This role serves as a key member of the Redfern Technical Team in the planning, implementation, and support for all events that take place within the Redfern Arts Center at Keene State College, supporting both the technical execution and artistic realization of all live events, conferences, concerts, meetings, etc. while working as part of a team to maintain the operational readiness of the Redfern’s technical equipment. This is an in-person role requiring on-site support for rehearsals, events, installations, and related preparation activities, including regular evening and weekend work based on performance and event schedules. Duties/Responsibilities Sets up, maintains and operates sound, lighting, stage and other technical equipment and  systems Ensures smooth operation of the technical aspects of all productions Monitors the condition of equipment including lighting, sound, and rigging equipment;   performs preventive maintenance on equipment Maintains current knowledge of all equipment Stays abreast of new technology and software relative to lighting, video, and audio   engineering. Additional duties as assigned by the Redfern Technical Director. Requirements Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience High School Diploma Experience in Theatre, Entertainment Technology, Lighting Design, or a related field, Ability to troubleshoot technical systems, solve problems in fast-paced production  e nvironments, and manage multiple projects simultaneously with limited supervision. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively with artists, designers, production staff, clients,   and colleagues while contributing to artistic and creative processes that enhance audience and   guest experiences. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a dynamic production environment, adapt   to changing priorities, work at heights using ladders, lifts, and catwalks, and safely lift and   move equipment weighing up to 50 pounds. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Strong organizational practices that promote clean, safe, and orderly workspaces. Demonstrated commitment to workplace safety, including the ability to model, implement, promote, and enforce safe working practices while providing leadership and direction to stagehands and production crews. Strong interpersonal, organizational, written, verbal, and computer skills, combined with professionalism, accountability, attention to detail, and ownership of projects through successful completion Preferred Qualifications: Experience in theatrical lighting, audio, live event production, or related entertainment technology environments. Working knowledge of theatrical lighting, audio, and video systems and infrastructure. Experience with ETC Eos control systems and networking environments or comparable professional lighting control platforms. Experience with the Midas family of audio consoles, including patching, routing, and cabling of audio systems, speakers, monitors, and microphones. Proficiency creating and modifying Lightwright documentation, and other production paperwork used for planning and execution. Demonstrated ability to read, understand, interpret, and implement technical riders, lighting plots, and related production documentation Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Cover Letter Compensation Pay Range: $25-$30 per hour Keene State College is located in the scenic Monadnock region of Southwest New Hampshire and is an affiliate of the University System of New Hampshire. Located approximately 2 hours from Boston or Hartford CT, and 4 hours from New York City, the region contains many opportunities to enjoy outdoor recreation, cultural events, and a strong sense of community. To learn more about Keene State College, the University System of New Hampshire, and the Keene community, please visit: https://www.keene.edu , https://www.usnh.edu/ or https://www.ci.keene.nh.us . EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Keene Salary Grade: Adjunct Hourly Staff 00"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Laboratory-Technician---Behavioral-Neuroscience--Animal-Research-_JR9326": {
      "title": "Laboratory Technician - Behavioral Neuroscience (Animal Research)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app The Laboratory Technician supports animal-based behavioral neuroscience research within the Department of Psychology, with primary responsibility for an alcohol self-administration research program using rodent models. The position coordinates daily experimental operations, including operant behavioral procedures, animal handling, and laboratory preparation necessary to execute substance-use research protocols. Working under the supervision of the Principal Investigator, the technician assists in implementing behavioral pharmacology studies, maintains animal research documentation, prepares experimental materials, and ensures compliance with institutional animal care and use standards. The role requires technical competency in animal handling, operant conditioning systems, and research compliance, as well as the ability to coordinate undergraduate research assistants involved in project workflows. This is a part-time (20 hours/week), grant-funded adjunct staff position. This position is not designated as essential staff during institutional curtailment periods. Duties/Responsibilities: Behavioral Experimentation & Operant Procedures (40%) Conduct rodent behavioral testing for alcohol self-administration studies. Operate and maintain operant conditioning chambers (e.g., lever press, dipper, cue delivery systems). Execute daily experimental sessions, including fixed ratio, progressive ratio, or demand procedures as required. Monitor behavioral responding and troubleshoot equipment or protocol issues. Assist in behavioral shaping, training acquisition, and reinforcement schedule implementation. Animal Handling & Research Support (25%) Handle and transport rodents in accordance with IACUC and institutional animal care guidelines. Assist with dosing procedures, including alcohol administration or pharmacological manipulations as approved. Support pre- and post-procedure monitoring of animals. Maintain accurate animal records, cage cards, and protocol logs. Coordinate with veterinary and animal care staff as needed. Laboratory Operations & Materials Preparation (15%) Prepare solutions, including alcohol dilutions and other experimental reagents. Set up experimental rooms and equipment prior to behavioral sessions. Maintain operant hardware, fluid delivery systems, and calibration procedures. Track laboratory supply inventory and coordinate restocking. Data & Compliance Documentation (10%) Maintain daily laboratory records and behavioral session logs. Ensure accurate documentation aligned with IACUC protocols and grant requirements. Organize experimental data files and assist with quality control checks. Support protocol renewals, amendments, and compliance reporting. Research Assistant Training & Coordination (10%) Train undergraduate research assistants in animal handling and behavioral procedures. Supervise RA participation during experimental sessions. Ensure adherence to laboratory SOPs, safety standards, and ethical conduct. Provide feedback to the PI regarding RA performance and training needs. Requirements: Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience: Bachelor's degree in Psychology, Neuroscience, Biology, or related field; or an equivalent combination of education and hands-on animal research experience sufficient to perform technical behavioral laboratory work after a reasonable training period. Required Licenses & Certifications: Eligibility to work with research animals under institutional IACUC approval. Completion of institutional animal care and use training upon hire Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Knowledge of behavioral neuroscience or psychopharmacology research methods. Competence in rodent handling and restraint techniques. Familiarity with operant conditioning systems and behavioral testing workflows. Ability to prepare drug and alcohol solutions accurately. Strong observational skills for monitoring animal health and behavior. Record-keeping precision aligned with regulatory compliance. Ability to train and oversee undergraduate assistants. Organizational skills for managing concurrent experimental cohorts. Commitment to humane animal care and research ethics. Other Requirements: Ability to work in animal research environments. Willingness to work flexible hours aligned with behavioral testing schedules. Medical clearance and occupational health compliance as required for animal work. Continued employment contingent on performance, project scope, and funding availability. Preferred Qualifications: Prior experience with rodent operant self-administration models. Experience with alcohol or drug reinforcement paradigms. Familiarity with progressive ratio or behavioral economic demand procedures. Experience with behavioral data systems (e.g., Med Associates). Surgical assistance or stereotaxic experience. Experience maintaining IACUC protocols or animal colony records Additional Details: Ability to work in animal research environments. Willingness to work flexible hours aligned with behavioral testing schedules. Medical clearance and occupational health compliance as required for animal work. Continued employment contingent on performance, project scope, and funding availability. Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Cover Letter Compensation Pay Range: $22.00 per hour Please be advised that this position is supported by external sponsor funding. As such, continued employment in this role is contingent upon the availability of those external funds. If, for any reason, the sponsor funding is reduced or discontinued, employment may be subject to modification or termination in accordance with applicable policies and procedures.  The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham Salary Grade: Adjunct Hourly Staff 00"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Adjunct-Faculty_JR9318": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app This is a course-by-course, part time position responsible for instruction of pre-licensure Nursing students in the clinical setting. The nursing clinical adjunct faculty instructor shall be responsible for the instruction and supervision of pre-licensure students during clinical learning activities at a cooperating agency. Duties/Responsibilities The nursing clinical adjunct faculty instructor shall be responsible for the instruction and supervision of pre-licensure students during clinical learning activities at a cooperating agency: Supervise and instruct prelicensure students in clinical environment Deliver instructional material in alignment with course objectives and student outcomes Utilize a variety of appropriate teaching strategies to promote student learning Evaluate and document student progress and provide relevant and timely feedback to students Requirements Candidates must meet one of the following conditions: Master’s degree in Nursing BS in Nursing, currently matriculated in an MSN or health care related graduate program BS in Nursing with extensive relevant experience Experience: At least two years of recent, relevant nursing experience in the specialty which you are applying for Licensure: Current unencumbered New Hampshire registered nurse license or a current and unencumbered multi-state registered nurse license issued by a compact state Preferred Qualifications: Experience in working with college age and non-traditional students Skill in working with culturally diverse constituencies in the academic environment Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Compensation Pay Range: $ 5,000-$7,500 per course The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham Salary Grade: Period Activity"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Manager--Dairy-Teaching-Research-Center_JR8473": {
      "title": "Manager, Dairy Teaching Research Center",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nReporting to the Director of the NH Agricultural Experiment Station, the incumbent will be responsible for leading the research, teaching, and outreach mission of the UNH Fairchild Dairy Teaching and Research Center. The manager oversees, stewards, and directly participates in the farm’s operational, personnel, and financial activities to ensure timeliness and success of animal management and care, infrastructure soundness, and interpersonal interactions. The manager supervises the full-time farm staff and student employees; is the primary coordinator of research projects, teaching activities (with a particular focus on enabling success of the UNH CREAM program), and engagement events on the farm, working with faculty, extension professionals, and staff; and works with external vendors and partners critical to effective dairy farm operations. In collaboration with the UNH Farm Services unit, the manager will coordinate manure management and crop storage activities. Through thoughtful and responsible leadership that emphasizes high standards for human and animal safety, strong and respectful interpersonal relationships with internal and external partners, and cost-effective operational management, the manager leads UNH Fairchild Dairy Teaching and Research Center through a culture that enables research that supports tomorrow’s New Hampshire dairy industry, impactful hands-on education that empowers tomorrow’s food system workforce, and state and industry recognition that UNH is a key destination for dairy science knowledge and innovation. Duties and Responsibilities Leadership of operations and people Provide overall leadership of the facility and the many diverse groups of stakeholders (researchers, instructors, students, student workers, residents, visitors, internal and external vendors and partners) who use and support the facility to meet the research, teaching, and engagement missions of UNH. Ensure that there is a collegial, communications-driven, and supportive culture of work that ensures that all those who use and visit the facility are welcomed and productive. Supervise full time employees, student workers, and adjunct staff. Be an active participant in regular meetings with other farm managers. Work with the NHAES operations manager to oversee the facility’s budget and provide responsible fiscal leadership. Work with the NHAES Director to identify, plan, and execute strategic investments to ensure long-term sustainability of the facility and its operations. Animal health and care Oversee the overall standards and protocols for animal care, healthcare, and data logging, ensuring that they follow industry best practices, align with UNH IACUC requirements and USDA requirements, and are coordinated with the UNH Attending Veterinarian. Identify and participate in continuing education of animal health and care and actively incorporate new knowledge and practices into the facility’s standard operating procedures. With the assistant manager, manage herd health and breeding. Provide training and instruction to staff, student workers, students, and others in identifying animal care issues and managing them. Ensure that veterinary supplies and records are regularly maintained, checked, ordered, and disposed of properly. Farm operations Participate in daily facility cleaning and animal feeding and milking chores. Ensure effective milk and animal sales. Working with UNH Farm Services, ensure effective manure management. Working with UNH Farm Services, ensure effective seasonal delivery and storage of feed. Ensure that there are sufficient student and adjunct staff employees and student residents to ensure effective farm operations. Equipment and facilities maintenance and repair Track and conduct preventative maintenance on farm machinery and infrastructure. Communicate and coordinate with internal (UNH Facilities, UNH Farm Services) partners and external vendors to ensure timely and effective repairs of facilities and equipment. Ensure that farm, office, and student living facilities meet safety, comfort, and presentability standards for employees; faculty, staff, and students; residents; and visitors. Assisting with research and teaching activities Working with researchers to coordinate, set up, and facilitate research projects. Working with instructors to provide guest lectures, educational activities at the farm, and coordinating classes and student clubs. Engaging with faculty, staff, extension professionals, and NHAES staff to organize outreach events at the farm for external stakeholders and audiences. Other duties Other related and relevant duties as assigned. Requirements Minimum Education & Experience Bachelor’s degree in animal science, dairy science, or a closely related field or an associate's degree with combined experience equal to 7 years of related experience. 5+ years experience working on a dairy farm, with demonstrated progression in responsibility and leadership. 4+ years of supervisory and leadership experience Preferred Qualifications Experience in advanced mechanical repairs and management. Experience with conducting or supporting agricultural research, including knowledge IACUC protocols. Experience in agricultural education and training. Knowledge and experience of overseeing building and other farm infrastructure construction and repair projects. Valid CDL. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Excellent communication skills and a commitment to timely and effective communication among employees and stakeholders. Supervisory and leadership skills needed to hire, train, and retain full-time and student employees. Experience in managing interpersonal interactions and leading supportive and collegial working environments for employees of different experience levels and skillsets. Training and experience in animal care and health topics, including artificial insemination and breeding. Knowledge and repair experience in basic mechanics. Experience in operating farm equipment and machinery (including milking equipment, feeding equipment, and mini loader) and ability to train other workers. Experience using computers for managing animal information, employee record keeping, and payroll. Sufficient strength and physical dexterity to perform duties and responsibilities of this job including heavy work (lifting up to 50 pounds) with exposure to inclement weather conditions for prolonged periods of time. Ability to wear and use appropriate personal protection equipment as necessary. Commitment to building and maintaining a culture of shared responsibility, team-based success, and continuous improvement. Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Current resume that demonstrates skillsets and experience relevant to the position description. Cover letter that provides a vision for leading a teaching and research dairy farm at a land-grant university and examples of relevant skillsets and experiences that demonstrate a strong fit with the position. Names and contact information (verified email and/or phone number) of three references. Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration. Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed. Priority Review Deadline Applications submitted prior to August 1, 2026. FTE Full-time, benefitted, salaried 1.0 FTE position. Please be advised that this position is supported by external sponsor funding. As such, continued employment in this role is contingent upon the availability of those external funds. If, for any reason, the sponsor funding is reduced or discontinued, employment may be subject to modification or termination in accordance with applicable policies and procedures.  The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Compensation Pay Range: $57,590.00 - $102,850.00 The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham"
