    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Facility-Scheduling-Coordinator_JR9279-1": {
      "title": "Facility Scheduling Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAs a professional within the Campus Recreation Department, this position fills an important role to ensure the facility schedules are maximized, ensure client needs are met, and event logistics are fulfilled to host successful events that provide a safe, positive experience for guests. Duties/Responsibilities Lead for scheduling all facilities managed by Campus Recreation (90%):   Coordinate facility schedule process from receiving requests, accommodating requests, deciding when to confirm requests, and making changes to reservations as requested.  Utilize effective customer service techniques when responding to requests.  Create estimates and agreements to external rental groups.  Track agreement process including renter’s insurance and signatures.  Create, track and maintain accurate invoices to each group in timely manner.  Coordinate with colleagues to provide hourly staff for external groups who rent facilities.  Ensure cooperative relationships between various user groups, departments and agencies. Facilitate regular meetings with stakeholders.  Attend select events to ensure events are successful.  Other duties as assigned as necessitated by the Division of Student Life.  Administrative duties (10%):   Manage use of resources including funding, personnel, facilities, and time.  Serve on Campus Recreation and university committees.  Participate in professional development opportunities to remain in the forefront of the field.  Assist Associate Director with projects as requested.  Requirements Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience: Associates degree preferred or 1-3 years of relevant experience in facility management. Collaboration skills with various student, faculty, staff, alumni, and external groups. Demonstrated effective communication skills, both written and verbal. Demonstrated effective use of software. Must be able to work flexible hours, including nights, weekends, and holidays. Must have valid driver license and/or qualify to drive university vehicles. Applicant Instructions:  Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/CV section of the application: (Maximum of 5 Documents) Resume/CV Cover Letter Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration. Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed. The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Compensation Pay Range: $17.57 - $28.96 The pay range for this position is listed above. Actual offer will be based on skills, qualifications, experience, and internal equity, in addition to relevant business considerations. More information on benefits can be found here: USNH Employee Benefits | Human Resources Location: Durham"
