    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Research-Intern_JR8972": {
      "title": "Research Intern",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-11\nPosted: Posted 25 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app The candidate will be working full time in a research study where fully autonomous robots are deployed in the homes of older adults with dementia to offer them assistance with activities of daily living. Duties/Responsibilities Writing new codes to expand the existing software framework Maintaining the current software Making deployment visits to participants home Troubleshoot the system whenever needed Collect and analyze data for dissemination Requirements Minimum Qualifications The candidate should have a bachelor's or master's degree in robotics or a related discipline Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Prior experience with robotics Knowledge of ROS2 Large scale robot software development Preferred Qualifications Some field deployment experiences Applicant Instructions Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the My Experience: Resume/Cover Letter section of your application: Resume/CV Cover Letter Contact Information for 3 Professional References Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration.  Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed. Compensation Pay Range $30.00 - $35.00/Hour Please be advised that this position is supported by external sponsor funding. As such, continued employment in this role is contingent upon the availability of those external funds. If, for any reason, the sponsor funding is reduced or discontinued, employment may be subject to modification or termination in accordance with applicable policies and procedures.  The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles 