    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Plymouth-State-University/NON-CDL-Shuttle-Driver_JR4883": {
      "title": "NON CDL Shuttle Driver",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-09-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app Plymouth State University is seeking Shuttle Drivers. Duties/Responsibilities Operate Shuttles to transport passengers over established routes according to time schedule. Perform vehicle pre-trip and post-trip safety inspections. Report hazardous road or travel conditions via two-way radio to dispatcher, as necessary. Fuel and clean vehicle upon completion of shift, as required. May be required to assist passengers in use of wheelchair lift and equipment, or in emergency situations by applying first aid. Perform related duties, as assigned. Requirements Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience : High School Diploma or GED Ability to pass DOT drug & alcohol testing under all required categories (pre-placement, random, suspicion, post-accident, return to duty, and follow- up) Required Licenses & Certifications : Valid operator’s license Ability to pass and maintain a valid DOT physical medical card Knowledge, Skills & Abilities : Knowledge of state laws governing the operation of motor vehicles Ability to communicate clearly and effectively with the dispatcher and public Sufficient strength and physical dexterity to perform duties and responsibilities of this position Other Requirements : Ability to perform vehicle pre-trip inspections outdoors in all types of weather; rain, snow, hot & cold weather Plymouth State University offers high-quality baccalaureate, graduate, and doctoral degree programs. Through research and innovative community partnerships, the University contributes to the economic, social, cultural, and environmental development of the North Country and Lakes Region of New Hampshire and beyond. Plymouth State University (PSU) is transforming the campus to create a first-of-its-kind university holistically organized around integrated clusters. Our goal is to provide a dynamic interdisciplinary and innovative learning environment. Students, faculty, staff, and community will connect to solve real-world challenges that will benefit people and organizations at all levels. We are a residential and comprehensive university with a warm and engaged learning community focused on teaching excellence and regional engagement. The University is located in the heart of the Lakes Region and White Mountains of New Hampshire and serves approximately 4,300 undergraduate and more than 2,000 graduate students. Surrounded by lakes and mountains, PSU’s 170-acre campus provides students with an outstanding natural laboratory for learning and an ideal setting for outdoor recreation. PSU has consistently earned national recognition for its commitment to community service, environmental sustainability, academic excellence, and employee wellness. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Location: Plymouth Salary Grade: Adjunct Hourly Staff 00"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Keene-State-College/Substitute-Teacher_JR4628": {
      "title": "Substitute Teacher",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-08-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app The Child Development Center (CDC), located on the Keene State College Campus in Elliot Hall, is a demonstration early childhood education site for Keene State College students, practicing professionals, and young children and their families. The CDC invites applicants for Early Childhood Substitute Teachers to work in partnership with the Center staff to achieve highest standards of quality for children, families, and college students. Duties/Responsibilities Support CDC staff in the implementation of the education and care program for young children. Implement daily curriculum, maintain and organize the learning environment, support and nurture young children, demonstrate kindness and respect in relationships with children, families and staff, and maintain confidentiality. Requirements Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience : Substitute teachers must meet NH Licensing associate teacher qualifications. Must be at least 18 years old, possess a high school diploma or equivalent, and complete at least 9 credits in related coursework with a child or human growth and development focus. Must have sufficient strength and physical dexterity to perform duties and responsibilities of this position, including lifting up to 50 lbs. Other Requirements : Upon hire, a CPR/First Aid course, background check for NH child care personnel, health record and NH Health and Safety courses will be completed.   Applicant instructions: Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the Resume/Cover Letter section of your application: Resume/CV Contact Information for 3 Professional References Unofficial Transcript Keene State College is located in the scenic Monadnock region of Southwest New Hampshire and is an affiliate of the University System of New Hampshire. Located approximately 2 hours from Boston or Hartford CT, and 4 hours from New York City, the region contains many opportunities to enjoy outdoor recreation, cultural events, and a strong sense of community. To learn more about Keene State College, the University System of New Hampshire, and the Keene community, please visit: https://www.keene.edu , https://www.usnh.edu/ or https://www.ci.keene.nh.us . EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Location: Keene Salary Grade: Adjunct Hourly Staff 00"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Keene-State-College/Group-Fitness-Instructor--Adjunct-_JR4327": {
      "title": "Group Fitness Instructor (Adjunct)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-08-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app Group Fitness Instructor will instruct fitness classes. Duties/Responsibilities Instruct in a relevant fitness class format: Yoga, Pilates, dance/Zumba, Spin / Indoor Cycling, Kickboxing, Barre, Hydrorobics, Pound, etc. Requirements Must be reliable and responsible with strong communication skills and a passion for group fitness. Experience in a relevant fitness class format preferred. Must attend any in-service training meetings and workshops scheduled.  Preference given to those certified by an approved national certification agency or those working toward certification. Please present a copy of fitness certification, and/or First Aid/CPR certification if available.  Applicant Instructions Applicants should be prepared to upload the following documents when applying online within the Resume/Cover Letter section of your application: Resume/CV Contact Information for 3 Professional References Copy of certification(s). Applications that are missing any of the required items may not move forward for consideration.  Additional uploaded documents not requested in the position announcement will not be reviewed. Keene State College is located in the scenic Monadnock region of Southwest New Hampshire and is an affiliate of the University System of New Hampshire. Located approximately 2 hours from Boston or Hartford CT, and 4 hours from New York City, the region contains many opportunities to enjoy outdoor recreation, cultural events, and a strong sense of community. To learn more about Keene State College, the University System of New Hampshire, and the Keene community, please visit: https://www.keene.edu , https://www.usnh.edu/ or https://www.ci.keene.nh.us . EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Location: Keene Salary Grade: Adjunct Hourly Staff 00"
