    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Keene-State-College/Men-s-Basketball-Assistant-Camp-Director_JR3197": {
      "title": "Men's Basketball Assistant Camp Director",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-05-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app The assistant camp directors are responsible for directing and direct oversight of the men’s summer basketball camps. They will help with daily oversight and operation of camp. During camp they will be the primary point of contact for any issues that arise from campers or family of campers and will ensure camp is operating smoothly. Duties/Responsibilities Oversight of camp on a daily basis Ensuring that camp is operating smoothly each day Managing both camper and staff issues Being available for any questions from campers or family of campers Coordination of camp activities Helping with layout of weekly/daily schedule of camp prior to start Assist in delegating responsibilities to staff Coaching/Teaching Helping coach/teach during games and stations when assistance is needed with other staff Minimum Qualifications Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience Bachelor’s degree Previous Keene State basketball camp experience This position will be a part of a Youth Skills Camp. Keene State College is located in the scenic Monadnock region of Southwest New Hampshire and is an affiliate of the University System of New Hampshire. Located approximately 2 hours from Boston or Hartford CT, and 4 hours from New York City, the region contains many opportunities to enjoy outdoor recreation, cultural events, and a strong sense of community. To learn more about Keene State College, the University System of New Hampshire, and the Keene community, please visit: https://www.keene.edu , https://www.usnh.edu/ or https://www.ci.keene.nh.us . EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Location: Keene Salary Grade: Adjunct Hourly Staff 00"
