    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Keene-State-College/Site-Supervisor_JR2769": {
      "title": "Site Supervisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-05-06\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app Site supervisor for external facility rentals. Duties/Responsibilities Act as on-site supervisor for external events. Ensure access to facility for all users. Act as on-site reference for an emergency. Minimum Qualifications High School Diploma Keene State College is located in the scenic Monadnock region of Southwest New Hampshire and is an affiliate of the University System of New Hampshire. Located approximately 2 hours from Boston or Hartford CT, and 4 hours from New York City, the region contains many opportunities to enjoy outdoor recreation, cultural events, and a strong sense of community. To learn more about Keene State College, the University System of New Hampshire, and the Keene community, please visit: https://www.keene.edu , https://www.usnh.edu/ or https://www.ci.keene.nh.us . EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Location: Keene Salary Grade: Adjunct Hourly Staff 00"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Keene-State-College/BW-Fitness-Specialist_JR2636-1": {
      "title": "BW Fitness Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-04-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app Campus Recreation & Fitness–BW Fitness Specialist position. Duties/ Responsibilities: Must be a declared major in HPMS Exercise Science and have completed the Practicum Leadership class. Desk responsibilities include answering the phone, scheduling fitness assessments and equipment orientations, answering members’ questions. Supervise the fitness center and enforce policies. Provide daily cleaning and upkeep of the facilities and equipment. Serve as a personal trainer for member clients. Understand all emergency procedures for the facility and be prepared to act in the event of an emergency. Must have current certification in American Red Cross first aid and community CPR/AED or equivalent. Must be able to work weekdays including early morning and evenings. Required Application Materials:   Resume Current first aid/CPR/AED certification Keene State College is located in the scenic Monadnock region of Southwest New Hampshire and is an affiliate of the University System of New Hampshire. Located approximately 2 hours from Boston or Hartford CT, and 4 hours from New York City, the region contains many opportunities to enjoy outdoor recreation, cultural events, and a strong sense of community. To learn more about Keene State College, the University System of New Hampshire, and the Keene community, please visit: https://www.keene.edu , https://www.usnh.edu/ or https://www.ci.keene.nh.us . EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Location: Keene Salary Grade: Adjunct Hourly Staff 00"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Assistant-Sailing-Director_JR2401": {
      "title": "Assistant Sailing Director",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-04-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app The Assistant Sailing Director supports the Sailing Director in managing the daily operations of the UNH Community Sailing Centre. This role assists with staff supervision, program coordination, and risk management to ensure a safe and engaging experience for participants. In the Sailing Director’s absence, the Assistant Sailing Director serves as the primary point of contact for program staff and participants. Duties/Responsibilities 1. Risk Management & Safety (50%) Applies risk management, conflict resolution, and behavior management strategies. Effectively communicates behavioral and safety concerns to counselors, participants, and parents/guardians. Documents incidents and accidents and provides follow-up for reports. Facilitates communication between staff and parents/guardians regarding camper behavioral concerns. 2. Program Administration & Staff Support (30%) Assists in the administrative and operational oversight of UNH Community Sailing Centre staff. Participates in the interviewing, training, and evaluation of staff, including pre-camp training sessions. Implements program changes, including but not limited to staffing adjustments and inclement weather activities. Creates organizational systems to track camp attendance. 3. Equipment & Facility Management (10%) Maintains inventory of boats and center equipment. Forwards recommendations for purchases to Campus Recreation professional staff. Assists with general boat maintenance and upkeep of the fleet. 4. Customer Service & Professionalism (10%) Presents a professional appearance and maintains a high standard of customer service. Develops and organizes daily activity rotations to enhance the participant experience. Minimum Qualifications Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience : Two Year post-secondary education. Required Licenses & Certifications : Employment contingent of the successful completion of a background check and the following Campus Recreation provided training: USNH Protection of Minors, ‘CPR, AED & First-Aid’, Bloodborne Pathogens, and Risk Management training. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities : Strong Supervision and Safety Awareness: Ability to maintain constant vigilance and ensure the safety and well-being of youth participants in waterfront settings. Program Implementation and Creativity: Knowledge of planning and delivering engaging, age- appropriate activities while fostering a fun and inclusive environment. Risk Management and Emergency Response Skills: Familiarity with risk management procedures, with the ability to respond effectively to routine and emergency situations, including administering basic first aid. Effective Communication and Team Collaboration: Strong interpersonal skills to communicate effectively with participants, parents, and colleagues, as well as the ability to work collaboratively within a team environment. Preferred Qualifications : Level 1 American Canoe Association Certification. Customer Service Experience: Demonstrated experience providing excellent customer service, including communication with parents and guardians. Background in Recreation or Education: Coursework or a degree in recreation, education, adolescent development, or a related field. Required Applicant Materials: Contact Information for 3 Professional References The University of New Hampshire is committed to providing a safe environment for all persons, including but not limited to children, and to prevent and respond to abuse, neglect and crimes against children. All UNH youth program staff shall be subject to a criminal background check as required by NH State Law. Staff and volunteers will also be required to complete periodic child safety training. The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Location: Durham Salary Grade: Adjunct Hourly Staff 00"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Equine-Facility-Summer-Stable-Worker_JR2266": {
      "title": "Equine Facility Summer Stable Worker",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-04-03\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app The Equine Facility at UNH depends on Stable Crew members to help care for our herd of 30+ horses. On-the-Job training is provided for all duties and advancement opportunities are available. 30-40 hrs. per week through the summer break. Duties/Responsibilities: Mucking Stalls and Paddocks Hauling and Stacking Hay Basic Horse Handling and Care Sweeping Floors and Cleaning Equipment Basic Herd Feeding Duties Summer facility maintenance Training Available for Advancement Opportunities include the following: Vehicle Driving Clearance and Operation Advanced Horse Handling and Grooming Advanced Herd Care and Basic Medical Care Leadership Opportunities for Tier 3 Staff Members. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities: Some knowledge and experience working with horses helpful but not required. Preferred Qualifications: Horse handling experience. The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Location: Durham Salary Grade: Adjunct Hourly Staff 00"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Mendums-Pond-Supervisor---Adjunct_JR2225": {
      "title": "Mendums Pond Supervisor - Adjunct",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-03-31\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app The Mendums Pond Supervisor is integral to the success and smooth operation of the Mendums Pond Outdoor Recreation Area. This position is responsible for facilitating staffing and daily operations, as well as overseeing facility and group rentals. The role requires working independently away from the Recreation Center while supervising summer staff. Strong communication with student staff, Special Events/Customer Experience (SECE) Intern, and the Outdoor Adventures (OA) Coordinator is essential. This position is considered essential staff and requires weekend availability during the summer. Duties/Responsibilities Facility and Program Oversight (40%) Oversee the boat and stand-up paddleboard rental program. Utilize Fusion software (training provided) to manage membership and rental sales, transactions, and data collection. Supervise Mendums Pond Attendants in check-in, boat rental, and membership sales. Oversee trails, picnic areas, and site group reservation usage. Staff Supervision and Training (30%) Supervise and support Mendums Pond Attendants during daily operations. Assist the OA Coordinator and SECE Intern with pre-season and ongoing staff training. Collaborate with other Campus Recreation student leadership positions to ensure smooth operations. Manage daily staff transportation from Hamel Recreation Center to Mendums Pond using Campus Recreation-provided vans (training provided). Safety and Risk Management (20%) Respond to emergencies, customer concerns, and weather-related challenges. Ensure adherence to Campus Recreation risk management policies and procedures. Maintain a safe environment for all participants and staff. Administrative Support (10%) Assist the SECE intern with summer scheduling and shift coverage. Support data collection, transaction records, and facility usage reports. Perform other duties as required. Minimum Qualifications Minimum Acceptable Education & Experience : 1 year post-secondary education  Drivers License  Previous experience in recreation, outdoor leadership, or customer service. Required Licenses & Certifications : CPR and First Aid Certification  In-house trainings: Risk Management, Bloodborne Pathogens, Concussion, Defensive Driving, Narcan, and Credit Card Security  All training provided by Campus Recreation.  Knowledge, Skills & Abilities : Strong leadership and supervisory skills. Effective communication, problem solving, and decision-making abilities. Ability to work independently and manage a dynamic environment. Proficiency with or ability to learn Fusion software. Other Requirements : Ability to work up to 20-25 hours per week. Weekend availability required (Mendums is open 12pm-6pm Friday-Sunday) Work Study eligible but not required. Must pass a criminal background check as required by NH State Law Preferred Qualifications: Experience managing outdoor recreation facilities or programs. Prior supervisory experience. Familiarity with outdoor equipment rental operations. Required Applicant Materials: Resume/CV Cover Letter The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Location: Durham Salary Grade: Adjunct Hourly Staff 00"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Indoor-Pool-Lifeguard-Supervisor--Adjunct-_JR1641": {
      "title": "Lifeguard Supervisor (Adjunct)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-03-18\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app *must be a current UNH Lifeguard to be eligible Lead the UNH Indoor and Outdoor Pool Aquatics Staff during daily operations in addition to internal and external facility rental group events. Lifeguard Supervisors work as a team leader as the head of the Lifeguard staff, with guidance and direction from Campus Recreation professional staff members and program assistants. ​ Duties/Responsibilities Safety & Risk Management (60%)  Follow all applicable safety rules and procedures to prevent accidents and ensure compliance.   Enforce and ensure all departmental policies are followed to maintain a safe and welcoming environment.   Provide appropriate first aid in conjunction with Lifeguard staff and risk management decisions when necessary.   Provide for the health and safety of participants, including ensuring that all teaching and practice areas are free of hazards and materials and equipment are safe. Provides emergency care and treatment as required until the arrival of EMS. Team Leadership & Communication (20%)  Work as part of a team to ensure smooth daily operations and positive staff collaboration.   Communicate effectively with lifeguards, facility staff, and patrons to address concerns and enhance the overall experience.   Facility Operations & Supervision (15%)  Serve as a representative of Campus Recreation to provide a safe aquatics environment and ensure that The UNH Outdoor Pool runs smoothly while providing exceptional customer service.  Implement operational procedures for ensuring water quality in compliance with NH RSA for operation of public bathing facilities.   Ensure on deck supervision during lifeguard breaks and operation outages.   Act as the main point of contact for community members, camps, teams, coaches, and university police.   Lead aquatics staff in opening and closing procedures, ensuring readiness and security of the facility. Maintain safety equipment and facility cleanliness for participant safety.   Takes direction from CPO and designated CREC professional staff Training, lead stations at in services & Supervisor meetings.   Additional Responsibilities (5%)  Perform other duties as assigned to support the success of the UNH Outdoor Pool.   Always presents professional appearance and attitude and maintains a high standard of customer service. Minimum Qualifications Prior experience in aquatics facility management or supervision.  Knowledge of risk management practices and emergency response protocols.  CPR, First Aid, and Lifeguard certification preferred.  Required Applicant Materials: Resume/CV Availability The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Location: Durham Salary Grade: Adjunct Hourly Staff 00"
    },
    "https://usnh.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/University-of-New-Hampshire--Main-Campus/Indoor-Pool-Private-Instructor--Adjunct-_JR1640": {
      "title": "Instructor (Adjunct)",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-03-18\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nUSNH Employees should apply within Workday through the Jobs Hub app Instructors may work in either the Indoor Pool or Outdoor Pool (or both) depending on the time of year. Instructors may teach Private or Group lessons. Job Duties: Apply American Red Cross Learn-to-Swim level curriculum and knowledge of other Red Cross water safety courses. Present professional appearance and positive attitude always and maintain a high standard of customer service Communicate regularly with participants and their parents/guardian, as appropriate, to ensure they are aware of progress. Enforce all aquatic facility policies, rules, and regulations.  Required Applicant Materials: Resume/CV Availability The University of New Hampshire is an R1 Carnegie classification research institution providing comprehensive, high-quality undergraduate and graduate programs of distinction. UNH is located in Durham on a 188-acre campus, 60 miles north of Boston and 8 miles from the Atlantic coast and is convenient to New Hampshire’s lakes and mountains. There is a student enrollment of 13,000 students, with a full-time faculty of over 600, offering 90 undergraduate and more than 70 graduate programs. The University actively promotes a dynamic learning environment in which qualified individuals of differing perspectives, life experiences, and cultural backgrounds pursue academic goals with mutual respect and shared inquiry. EEO Statement The University System of New Hampshire is an Equal Opportunity/Equal Access employer. The University System is committed to creating an environment that values and supports diversity and inclusiveness across our campus communities and encourages applications from qualified individuals who will help us achieve this mission. The University System prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or marital status. Location: Durham Salary Grade: Adjunct Hourly Staff 00"
